ns/9841fdad.json:3:  \"src\": \"colored horizontal runs in the left reference panel's active columns\",\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/annotations/9841fdad.json:4:  \"dst\": \"blank right panel's active columns\",\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/annotations/c3fa4749.json:3:  \"src\": \"4-connected multicolor objects inside a monochrome panel bbox that touch exactly one bbox side with a single marker color\",\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/annotations/dc46ea44.json:4:  \"dst\": \"translated guide marker branch anchor d in the upper panel\",\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/annotations/dc46ea44.json:6:  \"transform\": \"clear the lower panel; shift the five-pixel guide marker to the top; stamp s without rotation or recolor\",\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/f931b4a8/27/code.py:294:    - The upper-left and upper-right quadrants are control panels whose non-black counts encode output height and width.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/f560132c/9/code.py:19:#      cropped panels in a 2x2 layout with one-pixel separator gaps.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/f560132c/9/code.py:31:#    - The output layout uses exactly one separator width and always a 2x2 panel\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/f560132c/9/code.py:45:#      into four cropped quadrant panels\".\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/f560132c/9/code.py:46:#    - The new panel formatter assumes every geometric quadrant contains at least\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/f560132c/9/code.py:56:#    - Output-side panel placement is deterministic and non-overlapping because\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/f560132c/9/code.py:57:#      each cropped panel is pasted into its own row/column slot with a fixed\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/f560132c/9/code.py:64:#      cropped panels. This is strong enough that a viewer can notice the grid-\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/f560132c/9/code.py:71:#      between panels. No extra border color or textural overlay is added.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/f560132c/9/code.py:77:#      in panel layout.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/f560132c/9/code.py:79:#      the output is always panel-separated rather than the original full square.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/f560132c/9/code.py:350:    assert len(pts) > 0, \"cropped panel must contain foreground\"\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/f560132c/9/code.py:389:    Assemble scattered jigsaw pieces, decode a horizontal legend strip, and output separated quadrant panels.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/f560132c/9/code.py:399:    - Do not return the full recolored rectangle. Split that rectangle into its four geometric quadrants, tightly crop each quadrant's occupied cells, and place the four cropped panels in a 2x2 arrangement with 1-pixel separator gaps.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/f931b4a8/1/code.py:43:#       without turning the control panel into noisy scatter.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/f931b4a8/1/code.py:131:    - The top controls no longer encode size by pixel count, and they do not control their intuitive axis: the left panel contributes width while the right panel contributes height.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/annotations/ba1aa698.json:3:  \"src\": \"identical interior sprite instances inside the shared-border framed panels\",\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/annotations/ba1aa698.json:4:  \"path\": \"constant diagonal motion from panel to panel, continued one more standalone panel to the right; vertical offset is scaled from shared-border spacing to full panel width and rounded to the nearest row\",\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/annotations/ba1aa698.json:5:  \"trajectory\": \"stamp one copy of the sprite in the next framed panel at the extrapolated row and the same local columns\",\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/annotations/ba1aa698.json:6:  \"transform\": \"discard the previous panels; draw only the new single frame with the same frame and fill colors\",\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/annotations/ba1aa698.json:7:  \"grid_shape\": \"same height, width of one standalone panel\"\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/f560132c/19/code.py:24:#      field. Therefore the output is a two-panel image: left = rotated assembled square, right = tightly cropped\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/f560132c/19/code.py:28:#      four target colors reappear in both panels, which makes the fusion visible in 2-3 examples.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/f560132c/19/code.py:30:#    - The panel arrangement is fixed, so the task remains about reasoning over shape/color correspondences rather than\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/f560132c/19/code.py:42:#      deterministic panel compositor.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/f560132c/19/code.py:46:#    - Output legality is trivial because the two panels are generated on a fresh canvas with a fixed one-column gap.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/f560132c/19/code.py:48:#    - Side-by-side panels avoid clutter that would result from pasting the assembled square onto the same canvas as\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/f560132c/19/code.py:50:#    - The right panel is tightly cropped to the recolored source scene, so the preserved \"original positions\" remain\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/f560132c/19/code.py:52:#    - Because body colors and palette colors are disjoint, every source piece visibly changes color in the trace panel.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/f560132c/19/code.py:199:    assert len(pts) > 0, \"panel to crop must contain non-background cells\"\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/f560132c/19/code.py:204:def _compose_panels(left: np.ndarray, right: np.ndarray, bg: int = 0, gap: int = 1) -> np.ndarray:\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/f560132c/19/code.py:358:    - The legend now controls two linked outputs at once: its internal 2x2 patch still defines the color transfer, while its outer arm asymmetry determines the global rotation applied only to the assem