yu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/78332cb0/12/code.py:30:#      stages. A vertical chain does the analogous thing but arranges stage panels left-to-right.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/78332cb0/12/code.py:41:#      separator lines inside the chain, and output is no longer a single panel.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/78332cb0/12/code.py:50:#      bounded and cannot spill outside the target panel.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/78332cb0/12/code.py:51:#    - Stage-panel layout uses the axis orthogonal to the chain direction, with widths/heights sized\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/78332cb0/12/code.py:52:#      from the largest intermediate composite, so no panel clips or overlaps another.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/78332cb0/12/code.py:60:#    - Each stage panel contains only one composite object plus background, and stage panels are\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/78332cb0/12/code.py:236:def _render_stage_panels(stages: list[np.ndarray], orient: str, bg: int, sep: int) -> np.ndarray:\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/78332cb0/12/code.py:237:    \"\"\"Render intermediate composites as panels separated orthogonally to chain orientation.\"\"\"\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/78332cb0/12/code.py:270:        return _render_stage_panels(_iterative_stage_patches(ordered, \"h\", bg), \"h\", bg, sep)\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/78332cb0/12/code.py:273:        return _render_stage_panels(_iterative_stage_patches(ordered, \"v\", bg), \"v\", bg, sep)\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/78332cb0/12/code.py:295:    - Output all cumulative merge results as stage panels, separated from each other by full\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/78332cb0/12/code.py:481:    out = _render_stage_panels(_iterative_stage_patches(blocks, orient, BG), orient, BG, SEP)\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/7b5033c1/D9/2/code.py:28:#   的色段，长度 1 或 2 的短段直接删除，输出变成更短的单列。\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/7b5033c1/D9/2/code.py:35:#   生成器因此强制同时出现至少两个短段和两个长段，并保证删除像素数显著大于 0。\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/7b5033c1/D9/2/code.py:51:#   系统性消失，只剩下长段。因为输出仍是多色、而不是只剩一种颜色，这条规则比“多数颜色保留”\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/7b5033c1/D9/2/code.py:55:#   “相邻段颜色不同、长短段混合”来保证这一结构稳定且可见。\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/16de56c4/11/code.py:74:#   the corner strip reads as an instruction panel rather than another object.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/7b5033c1/D2/1/code.py:21:#    原逻辑会因为 A 更靠左上而从 A 开始，输出首色来自长度 7 的长段。\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/7b5033c1/D2/1/code.py:22:#    本变体要求从 B 开始，因为 B 所在色段更短，输出首色变成长度 3 的短段颜色。\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/7b5033c1/D2/1/code.py:37:#    生成器固定制造“短段端点 != 左上端点”的样本，使这条规则在 2-4 组样例中可见。\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/8b7bacbf/25/code.py:27:#      single-color loop frames, background cavities, plus one disconnected solid distractor panel whose only job\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/8b7bacbf/25/code.py:47:#    - Closed loops, the distractor panel, and distractor networks use empty-cell and halo checks so objects do not\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/8b7bacbf/25/code.py:57:#    - The palette stays small: one background color, one seed color, one line color, one distractor-panel color,\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/8b7bacbf/25/code.py:452:def _try_place_panel(canvas: np.ndarray, panel_col: int, rng: random.Random) -> bool:\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/8b7bacbf/25/code.py:479:                canvas[r0 : r0 + ph, c0 : c0 + pw] = panel_col\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/8b7bacbf/25/code.py:484:def _place_panel_far(canvas: np.ndarray, panel_col: int, corner: str, rng: random.Random) -> bool:\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/8b7bacbf/25/code.py:531:                canvas[r0 : r0 + ph, c0 : c0 + pw] = panel_col\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/8b7bacbf/25/code.py:579:def _place_big_panel_opposite(canvas: np.ndarray, color: int, corner: str) -> bool:\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/8b7bacbf/25/code.py:974:    panel_col = palette.pop()\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/8b7bacbf/25/code.py:983:    if _place_mode_breaker_slab(canvas, panel_col, corner) is None:\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/8b7bacbf/24/code.py:9:#     - \"seed 从单像素角落点改成 2-3 像素的边缘短段。\"\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/8b7bacbf/24/code.py:13:#     - \"top/bottom seed 是水平短段；left/right seed 是竖直短段。\"\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/8b7bacbf/24/code.py:22:#       - \"找全局只出现 2-3 次、且恰好组成边中央短段的颜色块。\"\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/8b7bacbf/24/code.py:39:#       - \"每个 seed color 只出现一次，且全部像素构成一个 4 连通短段。\"\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/8b7bacbf/24/code.py:40:#       - \"短段的所有像素都在同一条边上，并且精确落在该边中点模板。\"\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/8b7bacbf/24/code.py:51:#     - \"解题者从少量样例可直接看到：角落 seed 消失，改为边中央短段；线条总是从短段朝网格内部发出。\"\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ARC1_code/eval/b0f4d537.py:101:    - One panel contains only a sparse yellow skeleton; its bounding box is the output canvas.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ARC1_code/eval/b0f4d537.py:102:    - The other panel is a compact colored prototype made from horizontal and vertical line segments.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ARC1_code/eval/e345f17b.py:12:    - The grid has even width and splits into two equal-size panels.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ARC1_code/eval/e345f17b.py:13:    - The left panel contains a pink mask and the right panel contains a grey mask.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ARC1_code/eval/e345f17b.py:15:    - Align the two panels cell by cell.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ARC1_code/eval/e345f17b.py:16:    - Output one panel-sized black grid.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ARC1_code/eval/e345f17b.py:25:    assert width % 2 == 0, \"expected two equal-width panels\"\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ARC1_code/eval/e345f17b.py:33:    assert left.shape == right.shape, \"expected aligned left and right panels\"\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ARC1_code/eval/e345f17b.py:37:    assert left_colors == {Color.PINK}, \"expected a pink mask in the left panel\"\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ARC1_code/eval/e345f17b.py:38:    assert right_colors == {Color.GREY}, \"expected a grey mask in the right panel\"\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ARC1_code/eval/e345f17b.py:45:# Canvas and panel bounds.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ARC1_code/eval/e345f17b.py:59:    \"\"\"Return all left/right foreground counts that satisfy panel density bounds.\"\"\"\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ARC1_code/eval/d19f7514.py:12:    - The grid has even height and splits into two equal-size panels.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ARC1_code/eval/d19f7514.py:13:    - The top panel contains a green mask and the bottom panel contains a grey mask.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ARC1_code/eval/d19f7514.py:15:    - Align the two panels cell by cell.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ARC1_code/eval/d19f7514.py:16:    - Output one panel-sized black grid.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ARC1_code/eval/d19f7514.py:24:    assert height % 2 == 0, \"expected two equal-height panels\"\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ARC1_code/eval/d19f7514.py:25:    assert height > 0 and width > 0, \"expected nonempty panels\"\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ARC1_code/eval/d19f7514.py:33:    assert top.shape == bottom.shape, \"expected aligned top and bottom panels\"\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ARC1_code/eval/d19f7514.py:37:    assert top_colors == {Color.GREEN}, \"expected a green mask in the top panel\"\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ARC1_code/eval/d19f7514.py:38:    assert bottom_colors == {Color.GREY}, \"expected a grey mask in the bottom panel\"\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/58490d8a/26/code.py:57:#         - output is a cropped black panel with colored rows\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ARC1_code/eval/7c9b52a0.py:11:    \"\"\"Overlay the colored contents of same-sized blank panels after removing the dominant separator color.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ARC1_code/eval/7c9b52a0.py:15:      panels made from a common blank color plus sparse colored marks.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ARC1_code/eval/7c9b52a0.py:16:    - The panels are 4-connected regions of non-separator cells, and all panel\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ARC1_code/eval/7c9b52a0.py:19:    - Create one blank panel of that common shape.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ARC1_code/eval/7c9b52a0.py:20:    - For each input panel, copy every non-blank mark to the same relative\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ARC1_code/eval/7c9b52a0.py:21:      position in the output panel.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ARC1_code/eval/7c9b52a0.py:24:      transparent overlay of the small drawings inside its panels.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ARC1_code/eval/7c9b52a0.py:29:    panel_values = g[g != separator]\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ARC1_code/eval/7c9b52a0.py:30:    assert panel_values.size > 0\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ARC1_code/eval/7c9b52a0.py:32:    counts = Counter(map(int, panel_values))\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ARC1_code/eval/7c9b52a0.py:36:    panels = find_components(g, bg=separator, connectivity=4, monochromatic=False)\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ARC1_code/eval/7c9b52a0.py:37:    assert panels\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ARC1_code/eval/7c9b52a0.py:39:    boxes = [panel[\"bbox\"] for panel in panels]\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ARC1_code/eval/7c9b52a0.py:40:    panel_shapes = {(r1 - r0 + 1, c1 - c0 + 1) for r0, c0, r1, c1 in boxes}\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ARC1_code/eval/7c9b52a0.py:41:    assert len(panel_shapes) == 1\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ARC1_code/eval/7c9b52a0.py:42:    height, width = next(iter(panel_shapes))\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ARC1_code/eval/7c9b52a0.py:59:# Canvas/panel geometry.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ARC1_code/eval/7c9b52a0.py:76:    \"\"\"Choose per-panel mark sizes near the observed output coverage range.\"\"\"\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ARC1_code/eval/7c9b52a0.py:92:    \"\"\"Grow one connected mark inside the panel, avoiding already-used cells.\"\"\"\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ARC1_code/eval/7c9b52a0.py:117:def _gen_output_panel(h, w, mark_colors, sizes):\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ARC1_code/eval/7c9b52a0.py:131:def _place_panel_patches(out, separator, mark_colors):\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ARC1_code/eval/7c9b52a0.py:153:    \"\"\"Accept only examples whose solver output is exactly the composed panel.\"\"\"\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ARC1_code/eval/7c9b52a0.py:169:    out = _gen_output_panel(h, w, mark_colors, sizes)\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ARC1_code/eval/7c9b52a0.py:173:    grid = _place_panel_patches(out, separator, mark_colors)\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/58490d8a/1/code.py:75:#    - Output remains a sparse black legend panel with one active row every two\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/db0c5428/27/code.py:38:# - The D7 frame separation is also single-mode: one 15x9 left panel, one 15x24\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/db0c5428/27/code.py:39:#   right panel, and one solid divider column. A solver must infer both content\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/db0c5428/27/code.py:63:#   panel, so every copied block fits exactly once with no collisions.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/8b7bacbf/30/code.py:31:#     the row structure is fixed as [key, bg, fill] inside a small boxed panel.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/8b7bacbf/30/code.py:61:#     instruction panel rather than clutter.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ARC1_code/eval/93b4f4b3.py:21:    The input is split into two equal-width panels.  The left panel is a single-color\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ARC1_code/eval/93b4f4b3.py:23:    panel contains one monochromatic object for each hole-region.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ARC1_code/eval/93b4f4b3.py:26:    Return the left panel only.  For every background hole-region in the left panel,\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ARC1_code/eval/93b4f4b3.py:27:    normalize its mask to its bounding box, find the unique right-panel object with\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ARC1_code/eval/93b4f4b3.py:31:    The right-panel objects are not copied by position; their shapes are a palette\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ARC1_code/eval/93b4f4b3.py:32:    that names which color belongs in each matching left-panel hole.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ARC1_code/eval/93b4f4b3.py:65:PANEL_WIDTH_RANGE = (5, 6)  # Canvas width per panel.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ARC1_code/eval/93b4f4b3.py:132:    \"\"\"Choose panel dimensions and return derived height and inner width.\"\"\"\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ARC1_code/eval/93b4f4b3.py:133:    panel_width = random.randint(*PANEL_WIDTH_RANGE)\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ARC1_code/eval/93b4f4b3.py:137:    inner_width = panel_width - 2 * FRAME_THICKNESS\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ARC1_code/eval/93b4f4b3.py:138:    return panel_width, n_bands, band_height, height, inner_width\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ARC1_code/eval/93b4f4b3.py:147:def _gen_render_panels(panel_width, height, band_height, masks, frame_color, fill_colors):\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ARC1_code/eval/93b4f4b3.py:149:    output = np.full((height, panel_width), frame_color, dtype=int)\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ARC1_code/eval/93b4f4b3.py:154:        c0 = random.randint(FRAME_THICKNESS, panel_width - mask.shape[1] - FRAME_THICKNESS)\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ARC1_code/eval/93b4f4b3.py:159:    right = np.zeros((height, panel_width), dtype=int)\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ARC1_code/eval/93b4f4b3.py:164:        c0 = random.randint(FRAME_THICKNESS, panel_width - mask.shape[1] - FRAME_THICKNESS)\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ARC1_code/eval/93b4f4b3.py:179:    panel_width, n_bands, band_height, height, inner_width = _gen_layout()\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ARC1_code/eval/93b4f4b3.py:186:    output, left, right = _gen_render_panels(\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ARC1_code/eval/93b4f4b3.py:187:        panel_width, height, band_height, masks, frame_color, fill_colors\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ARC1_code/eval/66f2d22f.py:10:    Overlay the two equal input panels and mark positions that are empty in both panels.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ARC1_code/eval/66f2d22f.py:13:    - The input is a 2D grid whose width is split into two equal side-by-side panels.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ARC1_code/eval/66f2d22f.py:15:    - Each panel contains exactly one non-background foreground color.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ARC1_code/eval/66f2d22f.py:18:    - Align the left and right panels by row and column.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ARC1_code/eval/66f2d22f.py:19:    - A cell in the output is grey iff both aligned panel cells are background.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ARC1_code/eval/66f2d22f.py:29:    assert width % 2 == 0, \"expected two equal-width panels\"\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ARC1_code/eval/66f2d22f.py:41:    assert len(left_colors) == 1, \"expected one foreground color in the left panel\"\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ARC1_code/eval/66f2d22f.py:42:    assert len(right_colors) == 1, \"expected one foreground color in the right panel\"\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ARC1_code/eval/66f2d22f.py:43:    assert left_colors[0] != right_colors[0], \"expected distinct panel foreground colors\"\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ARC1_code/eval/66f2d22f.py:55:# Occupancy constraints for each panel and the grey output mask.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ARC1_code/eval/66f2d22f.py:130:def _gen_panel_colors(rng: np.random.Generator) -> tuple[int, int]:\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ARC1_code/eval/66f2d22f.py:141:    panel_width = int(rng.integers(*PANEL_WIDTH_RANGE))\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ARC1_code/eval/66f2d22f.py:142:    shape = (height, panel_width)\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ARC1_code/eval/66f2d22f.py:143:    n_cells = height * panel_width\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ARC1_code/eval/66f2d22f.py:150:    expected_out = np.full((height, panel_width), Color.BLACK, dtype=int)\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ARC1_code/eval/66f2d22f.py:153:    left_color, right_color = _gen_panel_colors(rng)\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ARC1_code/eval/66f2d22f.py:154:    inp = np.full((height, panel_width * 2), Color.BLACK, dtype=int)\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ARC1_code/eval/66f2d22f.py:155:    inp[:, :panel_width][left_mask] = left_color\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ARC1_code/eval/66f2d22f.py:156:    inp[:, panel_width:][right_mask] = right_color\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ARC1_code/eval/ea9794b1.py:9:    Composite four quadrant panels into one panel, resolving overlaps by a fixed positional layer order.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ARC1_code/eval/ea9794b1.py:12:    - The input is a 2x2 array of equal-size panels on a shared background.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ARC1_code/eval/ea9794b1.py:13:    - Each panel contains exactly one distinct foreground color.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ARC1_code/eval/ea9794b1.py:14:    - Corresponding cells in the four panels map to the same output cell.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ARC1_code/eval/ea9794b1.py:17:    - Create one output panel with the same shape as a single input panel.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ARC1_code/eval/ea9794b1.py:18:    - Paint the upper-left panel first, then lower-right, then lower-left,\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ARC1_code/eval/ea9794b1.py:20:    - Only non-background pixels are painted; later panels overwrite earlier\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ARC1_code/eval/ea9794b1.py:24:    - The four panels are transparent layers whose depth is determined by panel\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ARC1_code/eval/ea9794b1.py:30:    assert H % 2 == 0 and W % 2 == 0, \"grid must split evenly into four panels\"\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ARC1_code/eval/ea9794b1.py:31:    panel_h = H // 2\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ARC1_code/eval/ea9794b1.py:32:    panel_w = W // 2\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ARC1_code/eval/ea9794b1.py:33:    assert panel_h > 0 and panel_w > 0, \"panels must be non-empty\"\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ARC1_code/eval/ea9794b1.py:36:    upper_left = g[:panel_h, :panel_w]\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ARC1_code/eval/ea9794b1.py:37:    upper_right = g[:panel_h, panel_w:]\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ARC1_code/eval/ea9794b1.py:38:    lower_left = g[panel_h:, :panel_w]\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ARC1_code/eval/ea9794b1.py:39:    lower_right = g[panel_h:, panel_w:]\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ARC1_code/eval/ea9794b1.py:40:    panels = (upper_left, upper_right, lower_left, lower_right)\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ARC1_code/eval/ea9794b1.py:42:    panel_colors = [colors_present(panel, exclude={bg}) for panel in panels]\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ARC1_code/eval/ea9794b1.py:43:    assert all(len(colors) == 1 for colors in panel_colors), \"each panel must have exactly one foreground color\"\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ARC1_code/eval/ea9794b1.py:44:    assert len({colors[0] for colors in panel_colors}) == 4, \"panel foreground colors must be distinct\"\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ARC1_code/eval/ea9794b1.py:46:    out = np.full((panel_h, panel_w), bg, dtype=int)\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ARC1_code/eval/ea9794b1.py:47:    for panel in (upper_left, lower_right, lower_left, upper_right):\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ARC1_code/eval/ea9794b1.py:48:        mask = panel != bg\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ARC1_code/eval/ea9794b1.py:49:        out[mask] = panel[mask]\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ARC1_code/eval/ea9794b1.py:59:# Fixed panel colors and overlay priority.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ARC1_code/eval/ea9794b1.py:133:def _gen_fill_panel(\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ARC1_code/eval/ea9794b1.py:135:    panel_i: int,\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ARC1_code/eval/ea9794b1.py:139:    while int(masks[panel_i].sum()) < target:\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ARC1_code/eval/ea9794b1.py:142:        for r, c in _gen_coords(allowed & ~masks[panel_i]):\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ARC1_code/eval/ea9794b1.py:143:            trial = masks[panel_i].copy()\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ARC1_code/eval/ea9794b1.py:150:                if other_i == panel_i:\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ARC1_code/eval/ea9794b1.py:165:        masks[panel_i, r, c] = True\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ARC1_code/eval/ea9794b1.py:213:    \"\"\"Create panel masks containing all cells where that panel is visible.\"\"\"\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ARC1_code/eval/ea9794b1.py:215:    for color, panel_i in _COLOR_TO_PANEL.items():\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ARC1_code/eval/ea9794b1.py:216:        masks[panel_i] = out == color\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ARC1_code/eval/ea9794b1.py:221:    \"\"\"Sample final foreground counts for panels that still need filling.\"\"\"\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ARC1_code/eval/ea9794b1.py:223:    for panel_i in _NON_GREEN_PANELS:\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ARC1_code/eval/ea9794b1.py:224:        current = int(masks[panel_i].sum())\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ARC1_code/eval/ea9794b1.py:225:        allowed_count = int(allowed[panel_i].sum())\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ARC1_code/eval/ea9794b1.py:226:        non_green_allowed = int((allowed[panel_i] & (out != _GREEN)).sum())\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ARC1_code/eval/ea9794b1.py:231:        targets[panel_i] = random.randint(lo, hi)\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ARC1_code/eval/ea9794b1.py:236:    \"\"\"Check the panel density, connectivity, and pairwise-overlap constraints.\"\"\"\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ARC1_code/eval/ea9794b1.py:250:    \"\"\"Render the four panel masks into the 10x10 solver input grid.\"\"\"\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ARC1_code/eval/ea9794b1.py:252:    for panel_i, (r0, c0) in enumerate(_PANEL_ORIGINS):\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ARC1_code/eval/ea9794b1.py:253:        panel = np.zeros(_PANEL_SHAPE, dtype=int)\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ARC1_code/eval/ea9794b1.py:254:        panel[masks[panel_i]] = _PANEL_COLORS[panel_i]\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ARC1_code/eval/ea9794b1.py:255:        paste(inp, panel, r0, c0, transparent=_BACKGROUND)\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ARC1_code/eval/ea9794b1.py:275:    for panel_i in _FILL_PANEL_ORDER:\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ARC1_code/eval/ea9794b1.py:276:        if not _gen_fill_panel(masks, panel_i, allowed[panel_i], targets[panel_i]):\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ARC1_code/eval/73182012.py:9:    Recover the original quadrant from a four-way mirrored rectangular panel.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ARC1_code/eval/73182012.py:12:    - The input is a larger background grid containing one foreground panel.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ARC1_code/eval/73182012.py:13:    - The panel has even height and width.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ARC1_code/eval/73182012.py:17:    - Crop to the foreground panel's bounding box.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ARC1_code/eval/73182012.py:31:    panel = g[r0 : r1 + 1, c0 : c1 + 1]\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ARC1_code/eval/73182012.py:33:    h, w = panel.shape\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ARC1_code/eval/73182012.py:37:    source = panel[:mh, :mw]\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ARC1_code/eval/73182012.py:38:    assert np.array_equal(panel[:mh, mw:], source[:, ::-1])\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ARC1_code/eval/73182012.py:39:    assert np.array_equal(panel[mh:, :mw], source[::-1, :])\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ARC1_code/eval/73182012.py:40:    assert np.array_equal(panel[mh:, mw:], source[::-1, ::-1])\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ARC1_code/eval/73182012.py:45:# Canvas and mirrored panel geometry.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ARC1_code/eval/73182012.py:102:def _gen_make_panel(source: np.ndarray) -> np.ndarray:\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ARC1_code/eval/73182012.py:110:    panel = _gen_make_panel(source)\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ARC1_code/eval/73182012.py:114:    _gen_paste(inp, panel, r0, c0)\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ARC1_code/eval/d5c634a2.py:17:    \"\"\"Count the upward and downward red T tetrominoes into fixed green and blue tally panels.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ARC1_code/eval/d5c634a2.py:24:    - Make a 3x6 black output split into two 3x3 panels.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ARC1_code/eval/d5c634a2.py:25:    - For each upward T, fill the next corner slot in the left panel with green.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ARC1_code/eval/d5c634a2.py:26:    - For each downward T, fill the next corner slot in the right panel with blue.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ARC1_code/eval/d5c634a2.py:27:    - The slot order inside each panel is top-left, bottom-left, top-right, bottom-right.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ARC1_code/eval/d5c634a2.py:82:# Output tally panel geometry and retry limit.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/db0c5428/17/code.py:34:#      change legible instead of introducing many panels or placements.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/b10624e5/35/code.py:26:#   board, the solver returns only one target quadrant panel. To keep the crop\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/b10624e5/35/code.py:35:# - Returning one cropped target panel would be too ambiguous if the three\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/b10624e5/35/code.py:51:#   cropped 13x13 panel, not a 27x27 board.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/b10624e5/35/code.py:59:#   inside its quadrant, so the cropped output panel contains the entire result\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/b10624e5/35/code.py:66:#   quadrants, while the output always shows a single quadrant panel with a\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/b10624e5/35/code.py:73:# - The cropped output contains only one quadrant panel, which avoids the noisy\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/b10624e5/35/code.py:334:    Move one controlled quadrant motif into its opposite quadrant, then emit only that target panel.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/58490d8a/4/code.py:20:#     The output is still a black tally panel of the same size.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ARC1_code/eval/17cae0c1.py:17:    Decode each 3x3 grey symbol into its color and fill that symbol's whole 3-column panel.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ARC1_code/eval/17cae0c1.py:20:    - The grid is three rows high and is partitioned into adjacent 3x3 panels.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ARC1_code/eval/17cae0c1.py:21:    - Each panel is a black/grey symbol mask.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ARC1_code/eval/17cae0c1.py:25:    - Convert grey pixels in each 3x3 panel to a binary mask.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ARC1_code/eval/17cae0c1.py:27:    - Replace the entire 3x3 panel by the decoded color.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ARC1_code/eval/17cae0c1.py:30:    - The output preserves the panel positions but discards the internal black/grey drawing; each drawing is a compact symbol for a solid color.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ARC1_code/eval/17cae0c1.py:35:    assert height == 3, \"expected three-row symbol panels\"\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ARC1_code/eval/17cae0c1.py:36:    assert width > 0, \"expected at least one symbol panel\"\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ARC1_code/eval/17cae0c1.py:37:    assert width % 3 == 0, \"expected an integer number of 3-column panels\"\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ARC1_code/eval/17cae0c1.py:43:        assert block.shape == (3, 3), \"expected each panel to be 3x3\"\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ARC1_code/eval/17cae0c1.py:89:def _gen_panel_slice_17cae0c1(panel_i: int) -> slice:\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ARC1_code/eval/17cae0c1.py:90:    c0 = _GEN_PANEL_SIZE_17CAE0C1 * int(panel_i)\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ARC1_code/eval/17cae0c1.py:103:    \"\"\"Decode generated panels to the oracle output, rejecting unknown masks.\"\"\"\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ARC1_code/eval/17cae0c1.py:105:    for panel_i, c0 in enumerate(range(0, inp.shape[1], _GEN_PANEL_SIZE_17CAE0C1)):\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ARC1_code/eval/17cae0c1.py:106:        cols = _gen_panel_slice_17cae0c1(panel_i)\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ARC1_code/eval/17cae0c1.py:124:    \"\"\"Render selected codebook masks as black/grey panels in order.\"\"\"\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ARC1_code/eval/17cae0c1.py:127:        cols = _gen_panel_slice_17cae0c1(i)\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ARC1_code/eval/281123b4.py:13:    Overlay the four separated 4x4 panels into one 4x4 image using a fixed front-to-back panel order.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ARC1_code/eval/281123b4.py:16:    - The input is a 4x19 grid split by three full-height separator columns into four 4x4 panels.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ARC1_code/eval/281123b4.py:17:    - Each panel contains background 0 plus exactly one foreground color, and the four panel colors are distinct.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ARC1_code/eval/281123b4.py:20:    - Treat 0 cells in each panel as transparent.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ARC1_code/eval/281123b4.py:21:    - Stack the panels front-to-back in positional order: third panel, fourth panel, first panel, second panel.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ARC1_code/eval/281123b4.py:22:    - The output cell is the first non-background color visible at that position, or 0 if all panels are empty there.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ARC1_code/eval/281123b4.py:25:    - The four masks are already aligned; the only hidden information is their layer priority, which starts at the third panel and then proceeds cyclically.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ARC1_code/eval/281123b4.py:28:    assert g.shape == (4, 19), \"expected four 4x4 panels separated by three columns\"\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ARC1_code/eval/281123b4.py:35:    panels = []\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ARC1_code/eval/281123b4.py:36:    panel_colors = []\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ARC1_code/eval/281123b4.py:38:        panel = g[:, start : start + 4]\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ARC1_code/eval/281123b4.py:39:        colors = set(map(int, np.unique(panel))) - {0}\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ARC1_code/eval/281123b4.py:40:        assert len(colors) == 1, \"each panel must have exactly one foreground color\"\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ARC1_code/eval/281123b4.py:42:        assert color != separator_color, \"panel colors must differ from the separator color\"\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ARC1_code/eval/281123b4.py:43:        panels.append(panel)\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ARC1_code/eval/281123b4.py:44:        panel_colors.append(color)\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ARC1_code/eval/281123b4.py:45:    assert len(set(panel_colors)) == len(panel_colors), \"panel colors must be distinct\"\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ARC1_code/eval/281123b4.py:49:    for panel_index in VISIBLE_ORDER:\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ARC1_code/eval/281123b4.py:50:        panel = panels[panel_index]\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ARC1_code/eval/281123b4.py:51:        mask = (panel != 0) & (~filled)\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ARC1_code/eval/281123b4.py:52:        out[mask] = panel[mask]\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ARC1_code/eval/281123b4.py:59:# Grid geometry: four 4x4 panels separated by three uniform columns.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ARC1_code/eval/281123b4.py:66:# Overlay structure: order positions map to panel indices front-to-back.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ARC1_code/eval/281123b4.py:70:# Palette: one separator color plus one distinct foreground color per panel.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ARC1_code/