:538:    panel_items.sort(key=lambda item: (int(item[\"box\"][0]), int(item[\"box\"][1])))\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/271d71e2/D9/1/code.py:539:    expected = _pack_interiors(panel_items, BG)\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ARC1_code/train/760b3cac.py:82:# Canvas and panel geometry.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ARC1_code/train/760b3cac.py:117:    \"\"\"Paint the fixed source and direction-marker panels.\"\"\"\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ARC1_code/train/760b3cac.py:130:    dst_panel = out[SOURCE_ROWS, dst_c0 : dst_c0 + PANEL_SHAPE[1]]\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ARC1_code/train/760b3cac.py:131:    dst_panel[:] = np.where(np.fliplr(source_mask), SOURCE_COLOR, BG_COLOR)\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ARC1_code/train/363442ee.py:15:    - The source sprite is the non-background panel immediately left of the divider.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ARC1_code/train/363442ee.py:41:    left_panel = g[:, :divider_col]\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ARC1_code/train/363442ee.py:42:    sprite_rows = np.where(np.any(left_panel != bg, axis=1))[0]\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ARC1_code/train/363442ee.py:46:    assert sprite_r0 == 0, \"source sprite must start at the top of the left panel\"\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ARC1_code/train/363442ee.py:48:    sprite = left_panel[: sprite_r1 + 1, :]\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ARC1_code/train/363442ee.py:51:    assert slot_w == divider_col, \"left panel width defines the slot width\"\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ARC1_code/train/363442ee.py:55:    right_panel = g[:, divider_col + 1 :]\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ARC1_code/train/363442ee.py:56:    marker_colors = set(map(int, np.unique(right_panel))) - {bg}\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ARC1_code/train/363442ee.py:57:    assert len(marker_colors) == 1, \"right panel should contain exactly one marker color\"\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/a251c730/27/code.py:40:#     the source annulus out of a nested pair instead of scanning two disjoint panels.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/a251c730/3/code.py:43:#   - 视觉上和原题差异足够明显：目标输入框内部完全空白，而四边出现成对的彩色短段。\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/a251c730/3/code.py:47:#   - 固定 3 格短段比随机长段更整洁，且“取中点”几乎是肉眼直接可读的规则。\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/c4d067a0/23/code.py:21:#    - Replace the original scaled block projection with carrier panels. Each main-area panel is a 5x5 carrier square whose top-left\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/c4d067a0/23/code.py:25:#      diagonal marker pair -> infer hidden staircase shape -> match that shape up to rotation against panel cavities -> fill cavity.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/c4d067a0/23/code.py:34:#    - Solid monochrome NxN blocks are gone; the main-area objects are carrier panels with internal non-carrier masks.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/c4d067a0/23/code.py:35:#    - Color voting for one global base is no longer meaningful; the solver must identify panels by repeated carrier borders and then\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/c4d067a0/23/code.py:39:#    - Panels live on a separate step-6 lattice, each occupying 5x5 with a 4x4 work area, so panels do not overlap.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/c4d067a0/23/code.py:40:#    - The generator places the panel area strictly to the right of the legend and checks that every panel fits within the canvas.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/c4d067a0/23/code.py:42:#    - A human can see only two colored endpoints per legend symbol, then compare training outputs to notice that the filled panel\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/c4d067a0/23/code.py:54:#    - Metric 2: number of panel slots whose cavity signature differs from the legend slot at the same lattice coordinate. This must\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/c4d067a0/23/code.py:57:#    - Assumption: one non-bg color dominates as the panel carrier. Generator enforces a single carrier color over all panels.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/c4d067a0/23/code.py:60:#    - Assumption: every real panel is a 5x5 window with carrier last row/last column and a non-empty 4x4 work mask. Generator always renders that.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/c4d067a0/23/code.py:67:# === CFG: hidden shape / panel ===\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/c4d067a0/23/code.py:222:def _panel_masks(g: np.ndarray, carrier: int) -> list[tuple[int, int, np.ndarray]]:\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/c4d067a0/23/code.py:224:    panels: list[tuple[int, int, np.ndarray]] = []\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/c4d067a0/23/code.py:238:            panels.append((int(r0), int(c0), shape_mask.copy()))\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/c4d067a0/23/code.py:239:    assert panels, \"main area must contain carrier panels\"\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/c4d067a0/23/code.py:240:    return panels\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/c4d067a0/23/code.py:245:    Fill a panel array by reconstructing hidden staircase shapes from diagonal legend markers.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/c4d067a0/23/code.py:251:    - The main area contains repeated 5x5 carrier panels whose top-left 4x4 work areas expose either bg cavities or already colored versions of those staircase shapes.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/c4d067a0/23/code.py:255:    - Scan the carrier panels, extract the exposed shape mask from each work area, and match it to the unique legend shape up to rotation.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/c4d067a0/23/code.py:256:    - Fill every matching cavity with the legend color while leaving already correct panels unchanged.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/c4d067a0/23/code.py:260:    - Two diagonal endpoints define a hidden shape, and solving the task requires reconstructing that shape and recognizing the same mask after permutation and rotation in the panel field.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/c4d067a0/23/code.py:271:    panels = _panel_masks(g, carrier)\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/c4d067a0/23/code.py:273:    for r0, c0, shape_mask in panels:\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/c4d067a0/23/code.py:275:        assert sig in legend_map, \"every panel mask must match a legend shape\"\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/c4d067a0/23/code.py:288:def _render_panel(target: np.ndarray, top: int, left: int, carrier: int, mask: np.ndarray, color: int) -> None:\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/c4d067a0/23/code.py:340:        _render_panel(out, top, left, carrier, mask, piece_colors[src])\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/58f5dbd5/26/code.py:22:#      1. The destination side sits inside a rectangular panel whose background color `block_bg`\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/58f5dbd5/26/code.py:29:#      combo: the same red motif still matches the red block, but the holes must become the panel\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/58f5dbd5/26/code.py:46:#    - The generator must place a full rectangular destination panel, not just bare blocks, because\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/58f5dbd5/26/code.py:48:#    - The panel keeps a 1-cell margin around the outer block lattice, and 1-cell internal gaps are\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/58f5dbd5/26/code.py:51:#    - Motifs stay outside the panel and are axis-separated from it exactly as in the base task.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/58f5dbd5/26/code.py:53:#    - A human can infer the color rule because the destination panel repeatedly shows which color\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/58f5dbd5/26/code.py:58:#    - There are still only two clean regions in the input: one rectangular panel plus one motif\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/58f5dbd5/26/code.py:64:#      the blocks. The repeated panel cue keeps this learnable from 2-3 examples.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/58f5dbd5/26/code.py:69:#      Guarantee: the destination panel extends one cell beyond the outermost blocks and fills every\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/58f5dbd5/26/code.py:113:      side sits inside a separate rectangular panel of another color.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/58f5dbd5/26/code.py:114:    - Several solid 5x5 monochrome blocks appear inside that panel, each in a distinct color.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/58f5dbd5/26/code.py:126:      the destination-block region: use the panel background for carving, and output a tight mosaic.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/58f5dbd5/26/code.py:144:    # STEP 2) Recover the destination-panel background from the 1-cell ring around the blocks.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/58f5dbd5/26/code.py:349:    \"\"\"Choose a valid separated placement for destination panel and motif region.\"\"\"\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/58f5dbd5/26/code.py:368:            panel_h = dst_h + 2 * BLOCK_PANEL_MARGIN\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/58f5dbd5/26/code.py:369:            panel_w = dst_w + 2 * BLOCK_PANEL_MARGIN\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/58f5dbd5/26/code.py:384:                        if _can_split(H, W, panel_h, panel_w, mh, mw):\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/58f5dbd5/26/code.py:463:def _paint_destination_panel(\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/58f5dbd5/26/code.py:466:    \"\"\"Paint the rectangular block-side panel whose background defines the output.\"\"\"\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/58f5dbd5/26/code.py:467:    panel = np.full((dst_h, dst_w), int(block_bg), dtype=int)\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/58f5dbd5/26/code.py:468:    paste(grid, panel, dst_r, dst_c)\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/58f5dbd5/26/code.py:536:    \"\"\"Render the sampled destination panel/blocks and motif slots into the input grid.\"\"\"\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/58f5dbd5/26/code.py:542:    _paint_destination_panel(inp, dst_r, dst_c, dst_h, dst_w, block_bg)\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/a6f40cea/33/code.py:398:    Recover framed Manhattan paths as holes in a checkerboard panel while keeping the full canvas.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/a6f40cea/33/code.py:414:      target panel is a visible checkerboard on the original grid, and the path operation is\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/c4d067a0/10/code.py:17:#    two anchor blocks. Here the input is reframed as three panels:\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/c4d067a0/10/code.py:19:#    panels: [example enlarged result | query enlarged result]. A solver must first\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/c4d067a0/10/code.py:25:#    example panel would be redundant and the D8/3 layer would collapse. Their\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/c4d067a0/10/code.py:30:#    panels, then treats legend-only and block-only panels separately. It also no\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/c4d067a0/10/code.py:40:#    Humans can directly compare the first two input panels to see how a sparse\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/c4d067a0/10/code.py:42:#    panel. The second output panel differs visibly from copying because the query\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/c4d067a0/10/code.py:45:#    Each panel contains only one object family: singleton legend dots or enlarged\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/c4d067a0/10/code.py:224:    Learn how one legend panel is enlarged into a block panel, then render a second legend the same way.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/7b80bb43/15/code.py:14:# - Concrete behavior: the top-left corner contains three mini-panels A/B/C.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/7b80bb43/15/code.py:84:    panels = []\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/7b80bb43/15/code.py:86:        panels.append(g[0:EXAMPLE_H, start : start + PANEL_W] == fg)\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/7b80bb43/15/code.py:97:                pa, pb, pc = panels[a], panels[b], panels[c]\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/7b80bb43/15/code.py:112:                # B must be the \"fill first\" panel: it preserves A's hint while\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/7b80bb43/15/code.py:263:    - One foreground color forms both the main axis-aligned network and a tiny three-panel lesson in a corner.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/7b80bb43/15/code.py:272:    Key insight: The middle corner panel proves that some diagonal hint pixels survive the fill step, so the solver must remember which pixels were hints in the initial body instead of re-detecting them after filling.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/2ba387bc/25/code.py:25:#      * the output is no longer one final stack. It is a vertical strip of panels.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/2ba387bc/25/code.py:26:#        In each panel: left = current source grid, right = the accumulated 8-column\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/2ba387bc/25/code.py:28:#        valid 4x4 square per next panel.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/2ba387bc/25/code.py:34:#      * panel 0: source still contains F1,F2,S1,S2 plus distractors; destination empty\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/2ba387bc/25/code.py:35:#      * panel 1: F1 disappears from its source location and appears at destination rows 0:4, cols 0:4\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/2ba387bc/25/code.py:36:#      * panel 2: S1 disappears and appears at destination rows 0:4, cols 4:8\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/2ba387bc/25/code.py:37:#      * panel 3: F2 moves to rows 4:8, cols 0:4\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/2ba387bc/25/code.py:38:#      * panel 4: S2 moves to rows 4:8, cols 4:8\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/2ba387bc/25/code.py:39:#      * distractors never move in any panel\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/2ba387bc/25/code.py:48:#    - Generator forces 3-5 movable squares, so the panel strip shows several steps;\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/2ba387bc/25/code.py:60:#      move sequence panel by panel.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/2ba387bc/25/code.py:70:#      stack fits entirely inside each panel.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/2ba387bc/25/code.py:72:#    - A human sees the same distractors frozen in every panel while one 4x4 target\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/2ba387bc/25/code.py:74:#    - The left/right panel layout makes the \"take from source, place into output\"\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/2ba387bc/25/code.py:80:#    - Source and destination within each panel are separated by one blank column.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/2ba387bc/25/code.py:84:#    - D8 is quantified by `panel_count = valid_count + 1`; generator enforces\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/2ba387bc/25/code.py:93:#    - The solver assumes the panel layout is: source on the left, one blank column,\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/2ba387bc/25/code.py:178:def _render_panel(source: np.ndarray, stage: np.ndarray, bg: int) -> np.ndarray:\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/2ba387bc/25/code.py:200:    panels: list[np.ndarray] = [_render_panel(source, stage, bg)]\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/2ba387bc/25/code.py:204:        panels.append(_render_panel(source, stage, bg))\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/2ba387bc/25/code.py:206:    out_h = len(panels) * H + max(0, len(panels) - 1) * _PANEL_GAP\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/2ba387bc/25/code.py:207:    out_w = int(panels[0].shape[1])\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/2ba387bc/25/code.py:210:    for idx, panel in enumerate(panels):\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/2ba387bc/25/code.py:211:        paste(out, panel, int(r), 0)\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/2ba387bc/25/code.py:213:        if idx != len(panels) - 1:\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/2ba387bc/25/code.py:224:    3. Build a vertical strip of panels showing the source being emptied one square\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/142ca369/27/code.py:16:#      即每条射线最多 3 段。solver 仍对更长段序列稳健处理：第 4 段及以后按 1 格前缀显示。\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/58f5dbd5/11/code.py:72:#    - All repeated-color competition is confined to the motif panel, which remains a tidy 3x3 slot\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/58f5dbd5/11/code.py:73:#      lattice. The block panel stays unchanged and regular.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/a6f40cea/13/code.py:160:    Recover path-shaped holes inside a framed panel while preserving the full scene.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/142ca369/1/code.py:53:#    - 正交长段 + 90 度折弯与原题的对角锯齿有明显视觉差异，D1 的变化可直接观察。\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/a6f40cea/14/code.py:14:#      Example on a small panel:\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/a6f40cea/14/code.py:17:#      combo: checkerboard base + four fill anchors -> crop that panel and erase the L to the\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/a6f40cea/14/code.py:38:#    - The generator remains output-first: build the interior panel first, then derive outer traces.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/a6f40cea/14/code.py:53:#    - Distractors remain outside the frame, so the panel itself is not cluttered.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/a6f40cea/14/code.py:139:def _apply_corner_fill_anchors(panel: np.ndarray, fill: int) -> np.ndarray:\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/a6f40cea/14/code.py:140:    \"\"\"Return a copy of `panel` with the four inner-corner anchor cells set to `fill`.\"\"\"\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/a6f40cea/14/code.py:141:    out = np.array(panel, dtype=int, copy=True)\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/a6f40cea/14/code.py:150:def _infer_checker_hole_panel(inner: np.ndarray) -> tuple[int, int, int] | None:\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/a6f40cea/14/code.py:195:    Recover projected Manhattan paths inside a framed panel and punch them out of a checkerboard.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/a6f40cea/14/code.py:224:    panel_info = _infer_checker_hole_panel(out)\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/a6f40cea/14/code.py:225:    assert not (panel_info is None)\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/a6f40cea/14/code.py:226:    fill, base_even, base_odd = panel_info\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/a6f40cea/14/code.py:632:    base_panel = _make_checkerboard(H, W, int(base_even), int(base_odd))\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/a6f40cea/14/code.py:633:    anchored_panel = _apply_corner_fill_anchors(base_panel, int(fill))\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/a6f40cea/14/code.py:640:    grid[r0 + 1 : r1, c0 + 1 : c1] = anchored_panel\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/a6f40cea/14/code.py:642:    expected = anchored_panel.copy()\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/58f5dbd5/28/code.py:71:  panel and only in the special marker color.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/58f5dbd5/28/code.py:327:    - Fill all border cells, panel gaps, block gaps, slot gaps, distractor slots, and empty slots\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/a47bf94d/13/code.py:20:#    into two side-by-side panels: left shows only the source-side result, right shows\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/a47bf94d/13/code.py:43:#    left panel always keeps the source-side transforms while the right panel always\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/a47bf94d/13/code.py:44:#    shows the received complements shifted one side clockwise, making the panel split\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/a47bf94d/13/code.py:48:#    ring segments. No overlapping token regions are allowed, and the panel divider is\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/a47bf94d/13/code.py:226:def _render_dual_panels(base: np.ndarray, sources: dict[str, dict[str, object]], bg: int) -> np.ndarray:\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/a47bf94d/13/code.py:253:    Split a four-sided token router into a source panel and a destination panel.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/a47bf94d/13/code.py:263:    - In the left output panel, keep only the source-side result: solid becomes a\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/a47bf94d/13/code.py:265:    - In the right output panel, place the transmitted complement at the next clockwise\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/a47bf94d/13/code.py:267:    - The background router is copied into both panels, which are concatenated with a\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/a47bf94d/13/code.py:274:      different panels.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/a47bf94d/13/code.py:281:    return _render_dual_panels(base, sources, bg)\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/a47bf94d/13/code.py:381:    expected = _render_dual_panels(expected_base, expected_sources, 0)\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/2c181942/27/code.py:94:      槽型只占 hub 内侧中央的 4 格短段，不把整个内部铺满；四角与大部分腔体仍为空，\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/80a900e0/D12/1/code.py:10:#     variant: 先根据输入里“可见骨架”（钻石轮廓 + 外侧短段）推断应向哪些边扩展，再在扩展后的棋盘格上发射同样的射线\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/247ef758/34/code.py:31:#   - The right canvas is now a 15x15 panel with 2-3 separate thick frames:\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/247ef758/1/code.py:41:#   - 行段/列段用占位数组放置, 段之间至少留 1 格 frame_base, 避免视觉合并成更长段。\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/2ba387bc/46/code.py:42:          * left panel: original scene with all valid 4x4 objects removed\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/2ba387bc/46/code.py:44:          * right panel: the packed two-column destination stack\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/2ba387bc/46/code.py:56:       * erases A/B/C from the source panel, but leaves the distractor in place\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/2ba387bc/46/code.py:57:       * shows the cleared source panel plus the destination stack at right\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/2ba387bc/46/code.py:71:   - D8 is made visible by preserving the whole source panel in the output. Humans can see that\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/2ba387bc/46/code.py:117:   - `moved_pixels`: number of colored valid-object pixels erased from the source panel. Forced > 0.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/2ba387bc/46/code.py:125:     panel separated by exactly one background column. Generator and solver share this layout.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/2ba387bc/46/code.py:436:    - erase every valid object from the source panel\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/5545f144/17/code.py:39:#    Humans can spot repeated same-width panels in a tall strip because the actor\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/5545f144/17/code.py:43:#    repeated panel rhythm. The top panel is consistently the most resolved one.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/5545f144/17/code.py:45:#    No new colors are introduced. Every panel still contains one sprite plus\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/5545f144/17/code.py:350:    Key insight: The hard part is not the motion rule but discovering the hidden panel boundaries and noticing that the sparsest top slice is the latest state because time runs downward in reverse.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/247ef758/15/code.py:36:#   同一侧的段不能重叠；同色段还必须留 base-color 间隔，避免 solver 把它们并成一个更长段。\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/5545f144/21/code.py:14:#    - The leftmost segment is a legend panel that shows the exact sprite\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/5545f144/21/code.py:36:#    - The generator always includes a dedicated legend panel and now keeps at\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/5545f144/21/code.py:58:#    - Humans can spot the legend as a dedicated left panel and infer that the\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/5545f144/21/code.py:448:    - The leftmost segment is a compact legend panel containing one Up-oriented\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/5545f144/21/code.py:472:    assert len(segments) >= 2, \"expected a legend panel plus at least one snapshot\"\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/4c7dc4dd/23/code.py:27:#    - Output is a packed verification board containing two panels:\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/4c7dc4dd/23/code.py:54:#    - Packed output assumes both panels share the same interior size; all four\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/4c7dc4dd/23/code.py:74:#      panels never merge visually.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/4c7dc4dd/23/code.py:293:    - The puzzle is still an analogy, but now two cues must be fused: placement tells you which training sprite is \"before\" the other, and the final answer is a two-panel check that repeats the known destination next to the inferred test transformation.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/5545f144/6/code.py:22:#     * D19/0 changes the designated simulation panel to the left edge of that\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/5545f144/6/code.py:24:# - To keep the fusion operative instead of cosmetic, every panel gets one extra\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/5545f144/6/code.py:25:#   reachable branch marker. The leftmost panel is therefore locally ambiguous:\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/5545f144/6/code.py:27:#   time snapshots, while each injected branch appears in only one panel.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/5545f144/6/code.py:30:#     after adding one branch to every chronological panel:\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/5545f144/6/code.py:35:#   leftmost visible panel, filters that panel down to the markers shared by all\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/5545f144/6/code.py:37:#   solver that only continues the raw leftmost panel hits the injected branch.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/5545f144/6/code.py:44:# - Only one extra branch dot is added per non-start panel. That is enough to\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/5545f144/6/code.py:45:#   invalidate wrong start panels without making the pictures visually noisy.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/5545f144/6/code.py:49:#   reversed, and every non-left panel is intentionally non-deterministic.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/5545f144/6/code.py:54:# - `main()` now assumes the frame strip itself encodes the start panel: after\n/home/lixinyu/snap/n