anel\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/16b78196/D7/2/code.py:198:        if idx != len(panels) - 1:\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/16b78196/D7/2/code.py:207:    own panel with the corresponding bar segment.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/16b78196/D7/2/code.py:464:                return _pack_chain_panels(\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/16b78196/D7/2/code.py:473:    return _pack_chain_panels(best_scene, bar_occ, bar_color, bg, best_chains, bar_orientation)\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/16b78196/D7/2/code.py:901:    output = _pack_chain_panels(full_output, bar_cells, bar_color, bg, chain_records, orientation)\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/3dc255db/D7/1/code.py:21:#     - If there are multiple cups, concatenate those cropped panels along the cups' dominant\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/3dc255db/D7/1/code.py:58:#       cup panels; the branch depends on visible cup placement, not hidden metadata.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/7491f3cf/18/code.py:35:#    large canvas is now invalid. The new solver therefore extracts panels by 2D quadrant\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/7491f3cf/18/code.py:44:#    The border grid cleanly separates the four panels. The output crop removes irrelevant\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/7491f3cf/18/code.py:49:#    missing bottom-right panel.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/7491f3cf/18/code.py:185:    Composite two source panels into the missing fourth panel, then return only that panel.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/7491f3cf/18/code.py:188:    - A 13x13 grid containing four 5x5 panels in a 2x2 matrix with 1-cell borders.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/7491f3cf/18/code.py:189:    - Top-left panel: cue pixels = one 8-connected wall through the center plus one isolated\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/7491f3cf/18/code.py:190:      indicator pixel. Top-right panel: source tile 1. Bottom-left panel: source tile 2.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/7491f3cf/18/code.py:191:    - Bottom-right panel is blank in the input and represents the missing destination panel.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/7491f3cf/18/code.py:194:    - Flood-fill (4-connected) from the indicator inside the cue panel, blocked by the wall.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/7491f3cf/18/code.py:198:    - Return only the synthesized 5x5 destination panel, not the full 13x13 canvas.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/7491f3cf/18/code.py:201:    - The bottom-right panel is conceptually the same missing composite as in the original\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/7491f3cf/25/code.py:60:#    - 原 `b = most_common(t1)` 假设 panel1 是 source；现在背景色必须从 blank 面板恢复，\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/7491f3cf/25/code.py:64:#    - 原输出固定写回 panel3；现在改为写回唯一 blank 面板。\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/7491f3cf/25/code.py:74:#    - 解题者从 2-4 组样例中可以直接看到：网格总高宽在变，说明 panel size 和 border width 在变。\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/7491f3cf/25/code.py:122:    assert b_num > 0 and b_num % 3 == 0, f\"grid shape {g.shape} is incompatible with 4 panels\"\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/7491f3cf/25/code.py:130:    panel_mask = np.zeros(g.shape, dtype=bool)\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/7491f3cf/25/code.py:133:        panel_mask[rs, cs] = True\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/7491f3cf/25/code.py:134:    assert np.all(g[~panel_mask] == border), \"all non-panel cells must be border-colored\"\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/7491f3cf/25/code.py:396:    assert len(candidates) == 1, \"expected exactly one blank panel\"\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/7491f3cf/25/code.py:414:    assert len(matches) == 1, \"expected exactly one cue panel\"\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/7491f3cf/25/code.py:421:    assert len(ranked) == 2, \"expected exactly two source panels\"\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/7491f3cf/25/code.py:428:    Composite two source panels into the blank panel after jointly inferring geometry and roles.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/7491f3cf/25/code.py:431:    - Four square panels appear in one row inside a uniform border-colored frame.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/7491f3cf/25/code.py:434:    - Exactly one panel is blank, exactly one panel is the cue, and the other two are source patterns.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/7491f3cf/25/code.py:435:    - The cue panel contains one wall plus one 8-isolated indicator, all in a single cue color.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/7491f3cf/25/code.py:438:    - Recover `(panel_size, border_width)` from the whole-grid shape, then slice out the four panels.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/7491f3cf/25/code.py:439:    - Use the unique blank panel to identify the shared tile background color.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/7491f3cf/25/code.py:440:    - Use cue geometry to find the unique cue panel. Among the two remaining panels, the one closer to the cue index is tile1 and the farther one is tile2.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/7491f3cf/25/code.py:446:    - What changed is the prerequisite parsing: the solver must infer scale, separator thickness, and panel roles before it can apply that rule.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/7491f3cf/25/code.py:455:        assert get_bg(tile) == tile_bg, \"all panels must share one background color\"\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/7491f3cf/8/code.py:56:    - Tile assembly remains fixed: four 5x5 panels separated by 1-cell border columns.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/7491f3cf/8/code.py:65:    - Tile0 remains visually separate from the source panels because cue color differs from the\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/7491f3cf/8/code.py:67:    - Tile3 uses only tile background plus one shared foreground color, so the panel stays clean\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/7491f3cf/8/code.py:367:    Composite two same-colored pattern tiles into a fourth panel using flood-fill from an indicator pixel.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/7491f3cf/8/code.py:370:    - Four 5×5 panels in one row, border-separated.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/7491f3cf/24/code.py:23:    - The canvas remains a fixed 7x25 strip with four 5x5 panels.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/7491f3cf/24/code.py:24:    - Exactly one panel is the cue: 5 wall pixels plus 1 isolated indicator.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/7491f3cf/24/code.py:25:    - Exactly two panels are still single-foreground symmetric source patterns.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/7491f3cf/24/code.py:26:    - The remaining panel is the destination, but unlike the base task it is not\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/7491f3cf/24/code.py:29:        destination = the only panel already mixing both source colors\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/7491f3cf/24/code.py:30:        cue         = the only non-destination panel matching wall+indicator geometry\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/7491f3cf/24/code.py:31:        tile1/tile2 = the two remaining panels, ranked by distance to the cue\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/7491f3cf/24/code.py:39:      suppose the cue is at panel index 1, destination at index 0, and the source\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/7491f3cf/24/code.py:40:      panels at indices 2 and 3. Then tile1 is panel 2 and tile2 is panel 3 because\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/7491f3cf/24/code.py:47:      makes the destination visibly distinct from cue/source panels, which each have\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/7491f3cf/24/code.py:55:    - Base `t0,t1,t2,t3 = tiles` indexing is invalid because panel order now varies.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/7491f3cf/24/code.py:58:      turns the destination into a partially solved panel. The combo instead uses the\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/7491f3cf/24/code.py:66:    - Every object stays inside its original 5x5 panel, so no new geometric overlap\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/7491f3cf/24/code.py:74:    - Humans can find the destination because it is the only panel already showing\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/7491f3cf/24/code.py:90:    - Assumption: exactly one panel has two distinct non-background colors. Generator\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/7491f3cf/24/code.py:92:      source panels remain single-foreground.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/7491f3cf/24/code.py:93:    - Assumption: source panels each have exactly one non-background color. Generator\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/7491f3cf/24/code.py:174:def _panel_slice(j: int) -> tuple[slice, slice]:\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/7491f3cf/24/code.py:179:    return [grid[_panel_slice(j)].copy() for j in range(NUM_TILES)]\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/7491f3cf/24/code.py:275:    assert len(candidates) == 1, \"expected exactly one prefilled destination panel\"\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/7491f3cf/24/code.py:292:    assert len(matches) == 1, \"expected exactly one cue panel\"\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/7491f3cf/24/code.py:299:    assert len(ranked) == 2, \"expected exactly two source panels\"\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/7491f3cf/24/code.py:452:    assert len(set(backgrounds)) == 1, \"all panels must share the same background\"\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/7491f3cf/24/code.py:498:    Complete a partially prefilled destination by locating panel roles and composing\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/7491f3cf/24/code.py:502:    - Four 5x5 panels appear in one row inside a fixed 7x25 border frame.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/7491f3cf/24/code.py:503:    - One panel is a cue: a 5-pixel wall through the center plus one isolated\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/7491f3cf/24/code.py:505:    - Two panels are single-color symmetric source patterns sharing one background.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/7491f3cf/24/code.py:506:    - One panel is the destination: it already contains a sparse subset of the final\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/7491f3cf/24/code.py:510:    - Identify the destination as the only panel with both source colors present.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/7491f3cf/24/code.py:512:    - Among the two remaining panels, the source nearer to the cue is tile1 and the\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/7491f3cf/24/code.py:522:    - The destination is not blank, so panel roles cannot be read from fixed indices\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/7491f3cf/24/code.py:559:    out[_panel_slice(dst_idx)] = out_tile\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/7491f3cf/24/code.py:724:            g[_panel_slice(idx)] = tile\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/7491f3cf/24/code.py:727:        expected[_panel_slice(dst_idx)] = out_tile\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/a47bf94d/D15/2/code.py:16:#     - Input stays as the original single-panel wiring puzzle: one wire network,\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/a47bf94d/D15/2/code.py:22:#     - Left panel = \"source-side result\": only the endpoint that originally held\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/a47bf94d/D15/2/code.py:26:#     - Right panel = \"destination-side result\": only the opposite endpoint that\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/a47bf94d/D15/2/code.py:30:#         pre-placed far diamonds from the input remain only in this panel\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/a47bf94d/D15/2/code.py:36:#         left panel shows only the top diamond(A)\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/a47bf94d/D15/2/code.py:37:#         right panel shows only the bottom X(A)\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/a47bf94d/D15/2/code.py:38:#         both panels keep the same wire geometry, and a separator column marks\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/a47bf94d/D15/2/code.py:45:#       panels differ in token placement.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/a47bf94d/D15/2/code.py:49:#       the destination panel and pre-placed destination diamonds would leak into\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/a47bf94d/D15/2/code.py:50:#       the source panel. We therefore build a token-free base canvas first.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/a47bf94d/D15/2/code.py:52:#       could just remain in the copied output. The split-panel rule requires\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/a47bf94d/D15/2/code.py:53:#       distinguishing them so they can be removed from the left panel and kept\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/a47bf94d/D15/2/code.py:54:#       only on the right panel.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/a47bf94d/D15/2/code.py:57:#       removal keeps the two-panel construction clean and deterministic.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/a47bf94d/D15/2/code.py:66:#     - Left and right panels each contain only one role (source vs destination),\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/a47bf94d/D15/2/code.py:70:#     - Each panel keeps the original uncluttered wire drawing. Tokens are not\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/a47bf94d/D15/2/code.py:296:def _assemble_two_panels(left: np.ndarray, right: np.ndarray, bg: int) -> np.ndarray:\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/a47bf94d/D15/2/code.py:345:    source_panel = base.copy()\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/a47bf94d/D15/2/code.py:346:    dest_panel = base.copy()\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/a47bf94d/D15/2/code.py:349:        _stamp_pattern(source_panel, center, col, _DIAMOND_OFF)\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/a47bf94d/D15/2/code.py:351:        _stamp_pattern(source_panel, center, col, _X_OFF)\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/a47bf94d/D15/2/code.py:353:        _stamp_pattern(dest_panel, center, col, _DIAMOND_OFF)\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/a47bf94d/D15/2/code.py:383:                    _stamp_pattern(dest_panel, dest, col, _X_OFF)\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/a47bf94d/D15/2/code.py:390:                    _stamp_pattern(dest_panel, dest, col, _DIAMOND_OFF)\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/a47bf94d/D15/2/code.py:392:    return source_panel, dest_panel\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/a47bf94d/D15/2/code.py:397:    Split the routed token result into source-side and destination-side panels.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/a47bf94d/D15/2/code.py:406:    - Build two copies of the canvas: the left panel keeps only the source-end\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/a47bf94d/D15/2/code.py:407:      result (solid -> diamond, X stays X), while the right panel keeps only the\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/a47bf94d/D15/2/code.py:409:      remain there). Join the panels with a solid separator column.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/a47bf94d/D15/2/code.py:419:    return _assemble_two_panels(left, right, bg)\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/a47bf94d/D15/2/code.py:422:# --------------- generator (split_source_dest_panels) ---------------\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/a47bf94d/D15/2/code.py:705:    return _assemble_two_panels(left, right, bg)\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/7491f3cf/1/code.py:305:    Composite two pattern tiles into a fourth panel using a cross-shaped partition.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/7491f3cf/1/code.py:308:    - Four 5×5 panels in one row, border-separated.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/7491f3cf/1/code.py:315:    - The reached quadrant is the primary quadrant and copies panel 1 non-bg.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/7491f3cf/1/code.py:316:    - The diagonally opposite quadrant copies panel 2 non-bg.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/7491f3cf/1/code.py:317:    - The other two quadrants use the union of panels 1 and 2.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/9bbf930d/D2/1/code.py:65:   - 选择后的目标单元必须是 _has_corridor 为真的通道；builder 会显式打开该 turn cell 与延长段。\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/7491f3cf/3/code.py:311:    Composite two pattern tiles into a fourth panel using a curved wall and an indicator pixel.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/7491f3cf/3/code.py:314:    - Four 5x5 panels in one row, border-separated.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/7491f3cf/3/code.py:321:    - Inside -> take non-bg pixels from panel 1. Outside -> take non-bg pixels from panel 2.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/7491f3cf/3/code.py:322:    - Wall -> OR-combine the two panels at that position:\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/7491f3cf/3/code.py:323:      panel 1 wins if both are non-bg, otherwise keep whichever panel contributes a non-bg pixel.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/7491f3cf/3/code.py:326:    - The curved wall is both the separator and a fusion band: it is not owned by just one source panel.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/7491f3cf/11/code.py:16:#    Original task: panel 0 had 6 cue pixels, namely a 5-pixel wall plus one edge/corner indicator.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/7491f3cf/11/code.py:17:#    The solver flood-filled from that indicator, treated the reached side as panel-1 territory, and\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/7491f3cf/11/code.py:18:#    used panel 2 on the other side. In a concrete old example, a horizontal wall through row 2 plus\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/7491f3cf/11/code.py:19:#    an indicator at (0,2) made the top half come from panel 1 and the bottom half from panel 2.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/7491f3cf/11/code.py:23:#    indicator is at (1,2), then k=1 and panel-1 territory is the 5-cell cross\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/7491f3cf/11/code.py:24:#    {(2,2),(1,2),(2,1),(2,3),(3,2)}; if it is at (1,1), then k=2 and panel-1 territory expands to\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/7491f3cf/11/code.py:26:#    panel 2. The visible difference from the old task is that the split is no longer a straight or\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/7491f3cf/11/code.py:46:#    The cue tile is always legal because it places exactly two pixels inside a fixed 5x5 panel:\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/7491f3cf/11/code.py:53:#    panel 1 only on the small cross (k=1) or on the larger diamond (k=2).\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/7491f3cf/11/code.py:59:#    No arbitrary recoloring is introduced. Panel 1 and panel 2 keep their own single foreground\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/7491f3cf/11/code.py:71:#    - All four tiles share the same background color, and panel 3 is blank on input.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/7491f3cf/11/code.py:326:    Composite two pattern tiles into a fourth panel using a Manhattan-distance threshold cue.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/7491f3cf/11/code.py:329:    - Four 5×5 panels in one row, border-separated.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/7491f3cf/11/code.py:336:    - For each cell in panel 3, if its Manhattan distance to the center is <= k, copy panel 1's\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/7491f3cf/11/code.py:337:      non-background pixel there; otherwise copy panel 2's non-background pixel there.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/7491f3cf/11/code.py:353:    assert np.all(t3 == bg), \"panel 3 input must be blank\"\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/7491f3cf/11/code.py:357:    assert CENTER in cue, \"panel 0 must include the center marker at (2,2)\"\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/7491f3cf/7/code.py:19:#    - The layout stays identical to the original task: four 5x5 panels in one\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/7491f3cf/7/code.py:25:#    - The mapping rule changes from fixed panel index to area-vs-density:\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/7491f3cf/7/code.py:36:#      even though tile1 is panel1 and both sources have the same color.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/7491f3cf/7/code.py:47:#      panels share the same color.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/7491f3cf/7/code.py:84:#      panel1 and sometimes from panel2; the stable explanation is region size\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/7491f3cf/7/code.py:85:#      versus source density, not color or fixed panel index.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/7491f3cf/7/code.py:277:    Composite two same-colored source panels into tile3 using area-vs-density matching.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/7491f3cf/7/code.py:280:    - Four 5x5 panels are arranged in one row inside a 7x25 border frame.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/7491f3cf/7/code.py:290:      sparser pattern, regardless of whether that pattern came from panel 1 or 2.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/e3721c99/29/code.py:15:#    Two adjacent rectangles are legend panels; the opposite two are workspace regions. Each legend panel\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/e3721c99/29/code.py:16:#    has exactly two entries. The two legend panels reuse the same two hole counts but assign different\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/e3721c99/29/code.py:29:#    because each legend panel reuses the same hole counts with different colors. The original generator\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/e3721c99/29/code.py:35:#    The generator draws a full cross divider, places legends with a 1-cell inset inside their own panels,\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/e3721c99/29/code.py:119:        assert hc not in mapping, f\"local legend hole count {hc} must be unique within a panel\"\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/e3721c99/29/code.py:158:    assert len(legend_sides) == 1, \"legend panels must occupy exactly one side of the cross\"\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/e3721c99/29/code.py:318:    assert pairs, \"must have at least one legend hole pair that fits all panels\"\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/e3721c99/29/code.py:329:    kind = random.choice([\"vertical_panel\", \"horizontal_panel\"])\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/e3721c99/29/code.py:330:    if kind == \"vertical_panel\":\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/e3721c99/29/code.py:332:        panel_w = random.randint(*PANEL_SIZE_RANGE)\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/e3721c99/29/code.py:334:        div_c = panel_w if side == \"left\" else GRID_SIZE - 1 - panel_w\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/e3721c99/29/code.py:338:        panel_h = random.randint(*PANEL_SIZE_RANGE)\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/e3721c99/29/code.py:340:        div_r = panel_h if side == \"top\" else GRID_SIZE - 1 - panel_h\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/e3721c99/29/code.py:347:    if kind == \"vertical_panel\" and side == \"left\":\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/e3721c99/29/code.py:349:    elif kind == \"vertical_panel\" and side == \"right\":\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/e3721c99/29/code.py:351:    elif kind == \"horizontal_panel\" and side == \"top\":\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/7491f3cf/15/code.py:332:    Composite two pattern tiles into a fourth panel using a curved wall and an edge indicator.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/7491f3cf/15/code.py:335:    - Four 5x5 panels in one row, border-separated.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/7491f3cf/15/code.py:342:    - Inside region -> copy non-bg pixels from panel 1; outside region -> copy non-bg pixels from panel 2.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/7491f3cf/15/code.py:343:    - Wall pixels -> panel 1 if non-bg there; otherwise panel 2 may fill them when the wall is 4-connected.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/7491f3cf/15/code.py:347:      then use the indicator's actual edge location as the flood-fill seed to decide which side belongs to panel 1.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/7491f3cf/20/code.py:26:#    defines step 1, which composes src1+src2 into panel 4; the lower/right pair defines\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/7491f3cf/20/code.py:27:#    step 2, which composes panel 4+src3 into panel 5.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/7491f3cf/20/code.py:28:#    Example: if step 1 is a horizontal wall with indicator at (0,2), panel 4 takes src1 on\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/7491f3cf/20/code.py:30:#    (4,0), panel 5 then takes panel 4 on that indicator side and src3 elsewhere.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/7491f3cf/20/code.py:33:#    cases where panel 4 is effectively one source, where panel 5 ignores one of the three\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/7491f3cf/20/code.py:34:#    sources, or where the chained final panel matches a direct src1+src3 composition.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/7491f3cf/20/code.py:38:#    color, and a shared-center color. It also cannot stop after one composite; panel 4 is an\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/7491f3cf/20/code.py:39:#    explicit intermediate result and panel 5 is the final result.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/7491f3cf/20/code.py:41:#    The layout is a 7x37 strip: six disjoint 5x5 panels separated by 1-cell borders. The two\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/7491f3cf/20/code.py:46:#    makes the chain explicit: panel 4 demonstrates which cue structure acts first, panel 5\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/7491f3cf/20/code.py:50:#    three cue colors and one shared overlap pixel. This keeps panel roles separable instead of\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/7491f3cf/20/code.py:55:#    synthesis, which is visibly confirmed by panel 4 in every training pair.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/7491f3cf/20/code.py:223:    assert np.all(t4 == bg), \"panel 4 input must be blank\"\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/7491f3cf/20/code.py:224:    assert np.all(t5 == bg), \"panel 5 input must be blank\"\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/7491f3cf/20/code.py:333:    Chain two wall-guided composites across three source panels to fill two blank panels.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/7491f3cf/20/code.py:336:    - Six 5x5 panels in one row, border-separated.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/7491f3cf/20/code.py:344:    - Parse the two cue structures from panel 0.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/7491f3cf/20/code.py:345:    - Step 1: composite panel 1 and panel 2 using the first wall/indicator, producing the\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/7491f3cf/20/code.py:346:      intermediate panel 4.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/7491f3cf/20/code.py:347:    - Step 2: composite panel 4 and panel 3 using the second wall/indicator, producing the\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/7491f3cf/20/code.py:348:      final panel 5.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/e3721c99/18/code.py:105:def _swap_panel(grid: np.ndarray) -> np.ndarray:\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/e3721c99/18/code.py:106:    \"\"\"Apply the color-swap single-panel transform used on the right comparison panel.\"\"\"\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/e3721c99/18/code.py:132:def _compose_output(inp: np.ndarray, right_panel: np.ndarray) -> np.ndarray:\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/e3721c99/18/code.py:134:    return np.hstack([np.asarray(inp, dtype=int), np.asarray(right_panel, dtype=int)])\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/e3721c99/18/code.py:139:    Show the original panel beside its color-swapped resolution by hole-count matching.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/e3721c99/18/code.py:148:    - Read the legend as hole_count -> legend_color from the input panel.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/e3721c99/18/code.py:149:    - Build a transformed copy of that same panel: matching grey sprites take the legend color, unmatched grey\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/e3721c99/18/code.py:151:    - Output a width-doubled grid whose left half is the untouched input panel and whose right half is the\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/e3721c99/18/code.py:158:    return _compose_output(g, _swap_panel(g))\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/e3721c99/18/code.py:170:# -- legend panel --\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/e3721c99/18/code.py:264:    \"\"\"Place a full-row horizontal divider with legend panel above or below.\"\"\"\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/e3721c99/18/code.py:267:    panel_h = random.randint(*PANEL_SIZE_RANGE)\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/e3721c99/18/code.py:271:        div_r = panel_h\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/e3721c99/18/code.py:274:        r0 = random.randint(1, panel_h - 4)\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/e3721c99/18/code.py:276:        div_r = GRID_SIZE - 1 - panel_h\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/e3721c99/18/code.py:285:    \"\"\"Place a full-column vertical divider with legend panel left or right.\"\"\"\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/e3721c99/18/code.py:288:    panel_w = random.randint(*PANEL_SIZE_RANGE)\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/e3721c99/18/code.py:292:        div_c = panel_w\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/e3721c99/18/code.py:295:        c0 = random.randint(1, panel_w - 4)\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/e3721c99/18/code.py:297:        div_c = GRID_SIZE - 1 - panel_w\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/e3721c99/18/code.py:306:    corner: str, panel_h: int, panel_w: int, arrangement: str, total: int\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/e3721c99/18/code.py:314:        dr, dc = panel_h, panel_w\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/e3721c99/18/code.py:315:        r_min, r_max = 1, panel_h - cross_dim - 1\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/e3721c99/18/code.py:316:        c_min, c_max = 1, panel_w - along_dim - 1\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/e3721c99/18/code.py:318:        dr, dc = panel_h, n - 1 - panel_w\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/e3721c99/18/code.py:319:        r_min, r_max = 1, panel_h - cross_dim - 1\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/e3721c99/18/code.py:322:        dr, dc = n - 1 - panel_h, panel_w\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/e3721c99/18/code.py:324:        c_min, c_max = 1, panel_w - along_dim - 1\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/e3721c99/18/code.py:326:        dr, dc = n - 1 - panel_h, n - 1 - panel_w\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/e3721c99/18/code.py:334:    \"\"\"Place an L-shaped divider with the legend panel in one corner.\"\"\"\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/e3721c99/18/code.py:341:        panel_h, panel_w = cross, along\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/e3721c99/18/code.py:343:        panel_h, panel_w = along, cross\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/e3721c99/18/code.py:347:        corner, panel_h, panel_w, arrangement, total\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/e3721c99/18/code.py:657:    right_panel = _swap_panel(grid)\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/e3721c99/18/code.py:658:    if np.array_equal(right_panel, grid):\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/e3721c99/18/code.py:660:    expected = _compose_output(grid, right_panel)\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/7491f3cf/2/code.py:275:    - Four 5x5 panels in one row, border-separated.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/e3721c99/25/code.py:13:    legend_panel: still placed behind the divider near an edge or corner\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/e3721c99/25/code.py:65:  - Legend patches stay fully inside the legend panel with a one-cell inset from the\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/e3721c99/25/code.py:76:    from the legend's panel orientation, so the sample set visibly requires reading\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/e3721c99/25/code.py:269:    - Colored legend components live inside a divider-separated panel. Each legend is a\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/e3721c99/25/code.py:320:# -- legend panel --\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/e3721c99/25/code.py:443:    panel_h = random.randint(max(PANEL_SIZE_RANGE[0], cross + 2), PANEL_SIZE_RANGE[1])\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/e3721c99/25/code.py:447:        div_r = panel_h\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/e3721c99/25/code.py:450:        r0 = random.randint(1, panel_h - cross - 1)\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/e3721c99/25/code.py:452:        div_r = GRID_SIZE - 1 - panel_h\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/e3721c99/25/code.py:464:    panel_w = random.randint(max(PANEL_SIZE_RANGE[0], cross + 2), PANEL_SIZE_RANGE[1])\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/e3721c99/25/code.py:468:        div_c = panel_w\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/e3721c99/25/code.py:471:        c0 = random.randint(1, panel_w - cross - 1)\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/e3721c99/25/code.py:473:        div_c = GRID_SIZE - 1 - panel_w\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/e3721c99/25/code.py:482:    corner: str, panel_h: int, panel_w: int, line_h: int, line_w: int\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/e3721c99/25/code.py:486:        dr, dc = panel_h, panel_w\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/e3721c99/25/code.py:487:        r_min, r_max = 1, panel_h - line_h - 1\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/e3721c99/25/code.py:488:        c_min, c_max = 1, panel_w - line_w - 1\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/e3721c99/25/code.py:490:        dr, dc = panel_h, n - 1 - panel_w\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/e3721c99/25/code.py:491:        r_min, r_max = 1, panel_h - line_h - 1\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/e3721c99/25/code.py:494:        dr, dc = n - 1 - panel_h, panel_w\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/e3721c99/25/code.py:496:        c_min, c_max = 1, panel_w - line_w - 1\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/e3721c99/25/code.py:498:        dr, dc = n - 1 - panel_h, n - 1 - panel_w\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/e3721c99/25/code.py:509:    cross_panel = random.randint(max(PANEL_SIZE_RANGE[0], cross + 2), PANEL_SIZE_RANGE[1])\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/e3721c99/25/code.py:512:        panel_h, panel_w = cross_panel, along\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/e3721c99/25/code.py:515:        panel_h, panel_w = along, cross_panel\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/e3721c99/25/code.py:520:        corner, panel_h, panel_w, line_h, line_w\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/7491f3cf/16/code.py:8:#    Original: 4 panels are laid out in a single row and roles are hard-coded as\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/7491f3cf/16/code.py:9:#    cue, tile1, tile2, output. Fused variant: panels form a 2x2 matrix inside a\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/7491f3cf/16/code.py:10:#    13x13 grid. The cue panel can occupy any corner slot. The blank output panel\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/7491f3cf/16/code.py:12:#    neighbors, so it behaves like a \"middle\" panel in 2D adjacency terms. The\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/7491f3cf/16/code.py:13:#    remaining orthogonal neighbor of the cue is tile1 and the diagonal panel is\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/7491f3cf/16/code.py:19:#    blank panel can appear in different slots, but source-role recovery still\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/7491f3cf/16/code.py:25:#    - The output target is no longer \"last panel\".\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/7491f3cf/16/code.py:29:#    All four panels still occupy disjoint 5x5 windows separated by 1-cell border\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/7491f3cf/16/code.py:37:#    Each panel remains isolated inside its own 5x5 area. The matrix border makes\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/7491f3cf/16/code.py:40:#    - Exactly one panel is uniform blank.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/7491f3cf/16/code.py:41:#    - Exactly one non-blank panel is a valid cue tile.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/7491f3cf/16/code.py:188:    Composite two pattern tiles into a blank panel using a cue panel in a 2x2 matrix.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/7491f3cf/16/code.py:191:    - Four 5x5 panels arranged as a 2x2 matrix inside a 13x13 border-separated grid.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/7491f3cf/16/code.py:192:    - One panel is a cue: wall boundary (8-connected, through center) + one isolated indicator.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/7491f3cf/16/code.py:193:    - Two panels are source patterns. One panel is uniformly blank and is the output target.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/7491f3cf/16/code.py:196:    - Identify the blank target panel by content, not by fixed position.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/7491f3cf/16/code.py:197:    - Identify the cue panel by its wall+indicator structure.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/7491f3cf/16/code.py:198:    - Among the two remaining panels, the one orthogonally adjacent to the cue is tile1\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/7491f3cf/16/code.py:199:      and the diagonal panel is tile2. Flood-fill from the indicator, blocked by the wall:\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/7491f3cf/16/code.py:204:    - The matrix layout removes any reliable left-to-right panel order. Roles must be\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/7491f3cf/16/code.py:205:      recovered from panel content plus 2D slot adjacency.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/7491f3cf/16/code.py:216:    assert len(blank_slots) == 1, f\"expected one blank output panel, found {len(blank_slots)}\"\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/7491f3cf/16/code.py:230:    assert len(cue_candidates) == 1, f\"expected one cue panel, found {len(cue_candidates)}\"\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/7491f3cf/16/code.py:244:    assert int(get_bg(t1)) == bg and int(get_bg(t2)) == bg, \"all panels must share the same tile background\"\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/e3721c99/26/code.py:24:#       - The divider/panel structure is removed. Instead, there are exactly four\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/7491f3cf/9/code.py:434:    Composite two pattern tiles into the fourth panel using an asymmetric wall cue.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/7491f3cf/9/code.py:437:    - Four 5x5 panels in one row, separated by 1-cell borders inside a 7x25 grid.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/7491f3cf/9/code.py:440:    - Panels 1 and 2 are source patterns; panel 3 is blank in the input.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/7491f3cf/9/code.py:446:    - Inside cells copy non-background pixels from panel 1; non-wall cells outside inside\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/7491f3cf/9/code.py:447:      copy non-background pixels from panel 2.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/7491f3cf/9/code.py:448:    - Wall cells prefer panel 1 and use panel 2 only as fallback when the wall itself is\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/e3721c99/31/code.py:184:        panel = g[:div_r, :]\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/e3721c99/31/code.py:186:        panel = g[div_r + 1 :, :]\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/e3721c99/31/code.py:189:    colors = sorted({int(c) for c in np.unique(panel) if int(c) not in (bg, grey, DIV)})\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/e3721c99/31/code.py:191:        comps = components_mask(panel == int(color), connectivity=4)\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/e3721c99/31/code.py:259:        panel_r0 = 0\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/e3721c99/31/code.py:264:        panel_r0 = div_r + 1\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/e3721c99/31/code.py:270:        r = random.randint(panel_r0 + 1, panel_r0 + PANEL_HEIGHT - patch.shape[0] - 1)\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/7491f3cf/10/code.py:23:#    The canvas is still four 5x5 panels in one row. One panel is the cue:\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/7491f3cf/10/code.py:24:#    5 wall pixels plus 1 isolated indicator. Two panels are still symmetric\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/7491f3cf/10/code.py:25:#    source patterns. The remaining panel is now a partially prefilled output,\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/7491f3cf/10/code.py:28:#    Original task: panel 3 is all background, so the solver can hardcode roles.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/7491f3cf/10/code.py:30:#    panel that is not D1+D2-symmetric and treat it as the partially solved dst;\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/7491f3cf/10/code.py:31:#    finally assign the two symmetric source panels by distance to the cue\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/7491f3cf/10/code.py:43:#    - \"The output panel is the unique blank panel\" is invalid because D5 adds\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/7491f3cf/10/code.py:47:#    - Overwriting the whole dst panel without checking visible content is no\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/7491f3cf/10/code.py:57:#    - one panel with the special wall+indicator cue structure;\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/7491f3cf/10/code.py:58:#    - two panels with clear diagonal symmetry;\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/7491f3cf/10/code.py:59:#    - one remaining panel with only a few already-correct colored pixels.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/7491f3cf/10/code.py:75:#    - the two source panels are D1+D2-symmetric;\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/7491f3cf/10/code.py:81:#    - Assumption: among non-cue panels, exactly one is not D1+D2-symmetric.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/7491f3cf/10/code.py:84:#    - Assumption: the two source panels have distinct distances to the cue.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/7491f3cf/10/code.py:152:def _panel_slice(j: int) -> tuple[slice, slice]:\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/7491f3cf/10/code.py:157:    return [grid[_panel_slice(j)].copy() for j in range(NUM_TILES)]\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/7491f3cf/10/code.py:231:    assert len(matches) == 1, \"expected exactly one cue panel\"\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/7491f3cf/10/code.py:238:    assert len(dst_candidates) == 1, \"expected exactly one non-symmetric dst panel\"\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/7491f3cf/10/code.py:241:    assert len(source_indices) == 2, \"expected exactly two source panels\"\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/7491f3cf/10/code.py:242:    assert all(_is_d1d2_symmetric(tiles[idx]) for idx in source_indices), \"source panels must be symmetric\"\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/7491f3cf/10/code.py:249:    assert len(ranked) == 2, \"expected exactly two source panels\"\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/7491f3cf/10/code.py:306:    with all panel roles inferred from structure instead of fixed positions.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/7491f3cf/10/code.py:309:    - Four 5×5 panels in one row, border-separated inside a fixed 7×25 frame.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/7491f3cf/10/code.py:310:    - Exactly one panel is the cue: a 5-pixel wall through the center plus one\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/7491f3cf/10/code.py:312:    - Exactly two non-cue panels are D1+D2-symmetric source patterns.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/7491f3cf/10/code.py:313:    - The remaining panel is the destination, already prefilled with some correct\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/7491f3cf/10/code.py:318:      panel as the destination.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/7491f3cf/10/code.py:319:    - Among the two symmetric panels, the one nearer to the cue index is tile1\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/7491f3cf/10/code.py:326:    - The output panel is no longer the blank one. Role recovery now combines\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/7491f3cf/10/code.py:363:    out[_panel_slice(dst_idx)] = out_tile\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/7491f3cf/10/code.py:494:        g[_panel_slice(idx)] = tile\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/7491f3cf/10/code.py:497:    expected[_panel_slice(dst_idx)] = out_tile\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/e3721c99/27/code.py:23:#      panel 里出现 1/2/3 洞 legend，颜色分别是粉/黄/青；workspace 有一个红色 2 洞 sprite\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/e3721c99/27/code.py:26:#      融合后: 先找唯一贴边 divider，把图分成小 panel 与大 workspace；panel 中 1/2/3 洞\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/e3721c99/27/code.py:48:#    - divider、panel 与 workspace 的几何仍沿用原题布局器，blocked 区域禁止 sprite 落入。\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/e3721c99/27/code.py:52:#    - 人类能看到: panel 一侧有 2-4 个不同洞数示例，workspace 一侧有多色对象；输出里这些\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/e3721c99/27/code.py:146:    Find the unique border-touching divider component and split the grid into panel/workspace sides.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/e3721c99/27/code.py:149:      divider_mask, side_labels, panel_label, workspace_label\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/e3721c99/27/code.py:165:    panel_label = min(sizes, key=sizes.get)\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/e3721c99/27/code.py:166:    return divider_mask, side_labels, int(panel_label), int(workspace_label)\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/e3721c99/27/code.py:170:    g: np.ndarray, bg: int, divider_mask: np.ndarray, side_labels: np.ndarray, panel_label: int\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/e3721c99/27/code.py:177:        if int(side_labels[r, c]) != panel_label:\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/e3721c99/27/code.py:218:    divider_mask, side_labels, panel_label, workspace_label = _divider_and_regions(g, bg)\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/e3721c99/27/code.py:219:    legend_holes = _legend_holes(g, bg, divider_mask, side_labels, panel_label)\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/e3721c99/27/code.py:300:    \"\"\"Place a full-row horizontal divider with the legend panel above or below.\"\"\"\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/e3721c99/27/code.py:303:    panel_h = random.randint(*PANEL_SIZE_RANGE)\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/e3721c99/27/code.py:307:        div_r = panel_h\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/e3721c99/27/code.py:310:        r0 = random.randint(1, panel_h - 4)\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/e3721c99/27/code.py:312:        div_r = GRID_SIZE - 1 - panel_h\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/e3721c99/27/code.py:321:    \"\"\"Place a full-column vertical divider with the legend panel left or right.\"\"\"\n/home/lixi