e source panel.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/e3721c99/8/code.py:16:#    Original samples show a border-side legend panel and grey sprites scattered in the\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/7491f3cf/19/code.py:296:    Composite the two source tiles into the fourth panel under the combo rule.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/7491f3cf/19/code.py:299:    - Four 5x5 panels appear in a single row with 1-cell border separators.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/7491f3cf/19/code.py:301:    - Panels 1 and 2 are the aligned source patterns; panel 3 is blank input.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/7491f3cf/4/code.py:19:#     - The whole grid stays 7x25 with four 5x5 panels separated by border cells.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/7491f3cf/4/code.py:26:#     - D5/1 makes panel 3 unreliable: it contains cue-colored distractor pixels and\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/7491f3cf/4/code.py:32:#       If panel3 already shows a cue-colored speck there, solver must erase it too.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/7491f3cf/4/code.py:36:#       If panel3 already has a wrong cue-colored pixel there, solver must recolor it red.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/7491f3cf/4/code.py:51:#       7. at least two XOR-foreground cells left blank so panel 3 is not \"just cleanup\".\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/7491f3cf/4/code.py:59:#     - Ignoring panel 3 was optional in the blank-target task but becomes mandatory here\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/7491f3cf/4/code.py:60:#       because non-background pixels in panel 3 are guaranteed untrustworthy distractors.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/7491f3cf/4/code.py:62:#     - The generator only adds distractors inside panel 3, within the 5x5 bounds.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/7491f3cf/4/code.py:63:#     - Source patterns stay confined to their own panels and use a shared background color.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/7491f3cf/4/code.py:68:#     - Humans can read D5 from cue-colored specks in panel 3 that either vanish or change\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/7491f3cf/4/code.py:71:#       plus the two source colors, so the final panel remains cleaner than the noisy input.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/7491f3cf/4/code.py:78:#     - main() assumes panel 3 may be overwritten wholesale; generation explicitly constructs\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/7491f3cf/4/code.py:79:#       panel 3 as a mixture of wrong cue-colored pixels and background blanks.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/7491f3cf/4/code.py:349:    Reconstruct panel 3 for the combo variant by combining cue parsing with XOR composition.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/7491f3cf/4/code.py:352:    - Four 5x5 panels appear in one row, separated by a 1-cell-wide border.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/7491f3cf/4/code.py:359:      4-connected flood-fill partition are validated from panel 0.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/7491f3cf/4/code.py:360:    - Ignore the existing content of panel 3 completely.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/7491f3cf/4/code.py:366:      is now the occupancy XOR of tiles 1 and 2, and panel 3 must be overwritten wholesale\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/e3721c99/24/code.py:28:#    The task still stays in the original 30x30 divider+panel+workspace format, with four legend\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/e3721c99/24/code.py:43:#    The generator keeps the original blocked legend panel and workspace separation, places the\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/e3721c99/24/code.py:44:#    5x2 legend table fully inside the panel with a one-cell inset, and places sprites only in the\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/e3721c99/24/code.py:54:#    The legend is a small table isolated in the panel; sprites remain amorphous single components in\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/e3721c99/24/code.py:250:    - The grid still has a divider-colored panel and a larger workspace. Inside the panel sits one\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/e3721c99/24/code.py:336:    grid: np.ndarray, groups: list[list[tuple[int, int]]], panel_bbox: tuple[int, int, int, int]\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/e3721c99/24/code.py:338:    \"\"\"Place the grouped legend table inside the panel bbox.\"\"\"\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/e3721c99/24/code.py:339:    rmin, cmin, rmax, cmax = panel_bbox\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/e3721c99/24/code.py:342:    assert rmax - rmin + 1 >= h and cmax - cmin + 1 >= w, \"legend panel must fit the table\"\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/e3721c99/24/code.py:351:    \"\"\"Place a full-row divider with the legend panel above or below it.\"\"\"\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/e3721c99/24/code.py:352:    panel_h = random.randint(*PANEL_SIZE_RANGE)\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/e3721c99/24/code.py:355:        div_r = panel_h\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/e3721c99/24/code.py:359:    div_r = GRID_SIZE - 1 - panel_h\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/e3721c99/24/code.py:368:    \"\"\"Place a full-column divider with the legend panel on the left or right.\"\"\"\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/e3721c99/24/code.py:369:    panel_w = random.randint(*PANEL_SIZE_RANGE)\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/e3721c99/24/code.py:372:        div_c = panel_w\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/e3721c99/24/code.py:376:    div_c = GRID_SIZE - 1 - panel_w\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/e3721c99/24/code.py:383:    \"\"\"Place an L-shaped divider with a corner panel.\"\"\"\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/e3721c99/24/code.py:384:    panel_h = random.randint(*PANEL_SIZE_RANGE)\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/e3721c99/24/code.py:385:    panel_w = random.randint(*PANEL_SIZE_RANGE)\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/e3721c99/24/code.py:389:        dr, dc = panel_h, panel_w\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/e3721c99/24/code.py:397:        dr, dc = panel_h, GRID_SIZE - 1 - panel_w\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/e3721c99/24/code.py:405:        dr, dc = GRID_SIZE - 1 - panel_h, panel_w\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/e3721c99/24/code.py:412:    dr, dc = GRID_SIZE - 1 - panel_h, GRID_SIZE - 1 - panel_w\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/e3721c99/24/code.py:424:    \"\"\"Draw one divider layout and place the legend table in the panel.\"\"\"\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/e3721c99/24/code.py:427:        panel_bbox = _layout_full_horizontal(grid, blocked)\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/e3721c99/24/code.py:429:        panel_bbox = _layout_full_vertical(grid, blocked)\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/e3721c99/24/code.py:431:        panel_bbox = _layout_l(grid, blocked)\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/e3721c99/24/code.py:432:    _place_legend_stack(grid, groups, panel_bbox)\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/7491f3cf/5/code.py:27:#    - This combo keeps the same visual grammar (\"4 panels in one row, cue tile\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/7491f3cf/5/code.py:377:    Composite two source panels into the fourth panel after parsing a variable layout.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/7491f3cf/5/code.py:380:    - Four square panels appear in one row.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/7491f3cf/5/code.py:381:    - All outer borders and all inter-panel separators share one uniform color and\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/7491f3cf/5/code.py:383:    - Each panel has odd side length n. Panel 0 contains cue pixels (wall +\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/7491f3cf/5/code.py:384:      indicator), panels 1 and 2 contain source patterns, and panel 3 is blank.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/7491f3cf/5/code.py:387:    - Infer border width k and panel size n from the border bands, then extract\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/74