\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/7491f3cf/13/code.py:54:#      tile2 panel instead.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/7491f3cf/13/code.py:55:#    - `cue_set = non-bg(t0)`: invalid because panel 0 contains both cue and\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/7491f3cf/13/code.py:62:#    - All panels remain 5x5 and stay within the fixed 7x19 border frame.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/7491f3cf/13/code.py:65:#      so cue and source never overlap in the merged panel.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/7491f3cf/13/code.py:67:#    - A human can see three persistent clues at once: only 3 panels exist,\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/7491f3cf/13/code.py:68:#      the left panel mixes two colors, and the cue color has no isolated dot.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/7491f3cf/13/code.py:73:#    - Only one overlay is allowed in panel 0: cue over tile1, with disjoint\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/7491f3cf/13/code.py:75:#    - Exactly two non-bg colors appear in the merged panel, which makes the\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/7491f3cf/13/code.py:78:#    - Every sample uses the 3-panel merged layout.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/7491f3cf/13/code.py:84:#    - Exactly one foreground color in the merged panel forms a supported\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/7491f3cf/13/code.py:86:#    - The remaining foreground color in the merged panel is tile1's color.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/7491f3cf/13/code.py:91:#      validates that the merged panel exposes exactly one cue candidate, and\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/7491f3cf/13/code.py:278:    Composite two source tiles into the output panel using an implicit wall cue\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/7491f3cf/13/code.py:279:    that has been merged into the tile1 panel.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/7491f3cf/13/code.py:282:    - Three 5x5 panels in one row, border-separated, for a 7x19 grid.\n/home/lixi