6 is obvious because every sample contains several separated panels rather than one crop.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/269e22fb/15/code.py:78:#     - D17 is also visible because at least one panel shows a seam where opposite sides of the\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/269e22fb/15/code.py:86:#       samples where deleting one panel still leaves a unique solution. This keeps both fused\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/269e22fb/15/code.py:298:    Rebuild the full 20x20 motif from several shuffled crop-panels cut on a torus.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/269e22fb/15/code.py:301:    - The grid contains multiple 20-row carrier panels concatenated horizontally, with solid separator columns in a third color.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/269e22fb/15/code.py:302:    - Each panel reveals one rectangular two-color crop of the same hidden motif, and a crop may wrap across the motif's top/bottom edge, left/right edge, or both.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/269e22fb/15/code.py:305:    - Ignore the separator color, extract the visible crop from each panel, and treat either remaining color as the candidate foreground.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/269e22fb/15/code.py:311:    - The panels are shuffled wrapped fragments of one toroidal image, so the right answer is the only global torus stitching where all local matches agree on one orientation and collectively account for all 400 cells.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/269e22fb/15/code.py:320:def _make_panel(crop: np.ndarray, sep: int, display_top: int) -> np.ndarray:\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/269e22fb/15/code.py:322:    panel = np.full((20, w), int(sep), dtype=int)\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/269e22fb/15/code.py:323:    panel[display_top : display_top + h, :] = crop\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/269e22fb/15/code.py:324:    return panel\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/269e22fb/15/code.py:327:def _compose_input(panels: list[np.ndarray], sep: int) -> np.ndarray:\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/269e22fb/15/code.py:330:    for i, panel in enumerate(panels):\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/269e22fb/15/code.py:333:        pieces.append(panel)\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/269e22fb/15/code.py:337:def _leave_one_out_inputs(panels: list[np.ndarray], sep: int) -> list[np.ndarray]:\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/269e22fb/15/code.py:339:    for i in range(len(panels)):\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/269e22fb/15/code.py:340:        subset = [panel for j, panel in enumerate(panels) if j != i]\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/269e22fb/15/code.py:399:        panels: list[np.ndarray] = []\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/269e22fb/15/code.py:404:            panels.append(_make_panel(crop, sep, display_top))\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/269e22fb/15/code.py:406:        grid = _compose_input(panels, sep)\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/269e22fb/15/code.py:418:        leave_one_out = _leave_one_out_inputs(panels, sep)\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/269e22fb/21/code.py:51:#      the input is a horizontal strip of 2-4 shuffled carrier panels separated by solid\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/269e22fb/21/code.py:52:#      divider columns in a third color. Each panel reveals one rectangular crop from the same\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/269e22fb/21/code.py:57:#      D16 contributes the explicit many-input-one-output panelization, while D10 contributes\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/269e22fb/21/code.py:65:#    - Panel order is shuffled and the vertical padding inside panels is randomized so the\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/269e22fb/21/code.py:70:#      and recover panels before any motif matching.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/269e22fb/21/code.py:84:#    - The separator color appears only as panel padding and divider columns.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/269e22fb/21/code.py:85:#    - Each panel contains exactly one intact rectangle, with no internal masking noise.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/269e22fb/21/code.py:264:    Reconstruct the full 20x20 motif from several separated crop panels that overlap on the hidden source.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/269e22fb/21/code.py:268:    - Each non-divider panel contains exactly one visible rectangular crop from the same dihedral variant of the fixed 20x20 motif.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/269e22fb/21/code.py:269:    - There are 2-4 such panels; they are shuffled, vertically padded for presentation, and their source windows jointly cover the hidden 20x20 canvas.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/269e22fb/21/code.py:272:    - Ignore the divider color, split the strip into panels, and extract the visible crop from each panel.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/269e22fb/21/code.py:278:    - The panels are not independent clues; they are several windows into one hidden motif instance, so the correct answer is the only global assembly where all local matches agree under a common orientation and jointly cover the whole board.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/269e22fb/21/code.py:288:def _make_panel(crop: np.ndarray, sep: int, display_top: int) -> np.ndarray:\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/269e22fb/21/code.py:290:    panel = np.full((_CANVAS, w), int(sep), dtype=int)\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/269e22fb/21/code.py:291:    panel[display_top : display_top + h, :] = crop\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/269e22fb/21/code.py:292:    return panel\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/269e22fb/21/code.py:295:def _compose_input(panels: list[np.ndarray], sep: int) -> np.ndarray:\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/269e22fb/21/code.py:298:    for idx, panel in enumerate(panels):\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/269e22fb/21/code.py:301:        pieces.append(panel)\n/ho