:375:        dr, dc = n - 1 - panel_h, panel_w\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/e3721c99/D7/1/code.py:377:        c_min, c_max = 1, panel_w - along_dim - 1\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/e3721c99/D7/1/code.py:379:        dr, dc = n - 1 - panel_h, n - 1 - panel_w\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/e3721c99/D7/1/code.py:387:    \"\"\"Place an L-shaped divider with legend panel in one corner.\"\"\"\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/e3721c99/D7/1/code.py:394:        panel_h, panel_w = cross, along\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/e3721c99/D7/1/code.py:396:        panel_h, panel_w = along, cross\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/e3721c99/D7/1/code.py:400:        corner, panel_h, panel_w, arrangement, total\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/b0039139/D9/1/code.py:95:    - Section 3 is a black palette panel containing one 2x2 code: top-left/bottom-right = foreground,\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/b0039139/D9/1/code.py:165:    panel = np.zeros((h, w), dtype=int)\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/b0039139/D9/1/code.py:169:    panel[r0 : r0 + 2, c0 : c0 + 2] = np.array(\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/b0039139/D9/1/code.py:173:    return panel\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/3e6067c3/D7/2/code.py:49:#      same local bridge motif repeats as a row of separate panels. The divider columns make the new\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/3e6067c3/D7/2/code.py:53:#      Full-height divider columns keep panels readable even when successive frames have different\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/3e6067c3/D7/2/code.py:58:#      new concept the solver must infer is panelization.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/b0039139/D8/2/code.py:63:#   keeps the meaningful shape entirely inside the black-bordered template panel.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/b0039139/D8/2/code.py:163:    - Section 1 is a black template panel containing yellow (4) shape pixels; section 2 is a\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/b0039139/D3/1/code.py:83:    - Section 1 is a black-background shape template; section 2 is a multi-color counting panel.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/edb79dae/29/code.py:19:#        left  panel: a 2x2 \"base palette\" of four solid 3x3 color swatches;\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/edb79dae/29/code.py:20:#        right panel: a 2x2 \"modifier palette\" of four 3x3 glyphs on background.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/edb79dae/29/code.py:22:#      That region indexes *both* panels. The base panel contributes the default region color. The\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/edb79dae/29/code.py:30:#      Difference: recolor is no longer a single color-key lookup nor a direct one-panel region map.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/edb79dae/29/code.py:66:#    - Because the composed mapping is a non-identity permutation, the right panel cannot be ignored:\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/edb79dae/29/code.py:67:#      reading only the left panel gives the wrong recolor in the same sample.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/edb79dae/29/code.py:70:#    - `_read_base_panel` assumes each 3x3 swatch is solid and non-background. Generator constructs\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/edb79dae/29/code.py:72:#    - `_read_modifier_panel` assumes each 3x3 block matches one of four hard-coded masks. Generator\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/edb79dae/29/code.py:179:def _extract_panel_block(panel: np.ndarray, region: tuple[int, int]) -> np.ndarray:\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/edb79dae/29/code.py:181:    return panel[r0 : r0 + PANEL_BLOCK, c0 : c0 + PANEL_BLOCK]\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/edb79dae/29/code.py:184:def _read_base_panel(g: np.ndarray, bg: int) -> dict[tuple[int, int], int]:\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/edb79dae/29/code.py:185:    \"\"\"Read the fixed 7x7 base color panel from the top-left corner.\"\"\"\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/edb79dae/29/code.py:187:    panel = g[BASE_PANEL_R0 : BASE_PANEL_R0 + PANEL_SIZE, BASE_PANEL_C0 : BASE_PANEL_C0 + PANEL_SIZE]\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/edb79dae/29/code.py:188:    assert np.all(panel[3, :] == bg) and np.all(panel[:, 3] == bg), \"base panel must contain a background cross\"\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/edb79dae/29/code.py:191:        block = _extract_panel_block(panel, region)\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/edb79dae/29/code.py:193:        assert len(cols) == 1, \"base panel entries must be solid\"\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/edb79dae/29/code.py:195:        assert col != bg, \"base panel entries cannot use the background color\"\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/edb79dae/29/code.py:200:def _read_modifier_panel(g: np.ndarray, bg: int) -> dict[tuple[int, int], tuple[int, int]]:\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/edb79dae/29/code.py:201:    \"\"\"Read the fixed 7x7 modifier glyph panel from the top-left legend area.\"\"\"\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/edb79dae/29/code.py:203:    assert np.all(g[:LEGEND_H, PANEL_SIZE] == bg), \"legend panels must be separated by one background column\"\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/edb79dae/29/code.py:204:    panel = g[MOD_PANEL_R0 : MOD_PANEL_R0 + PANEL_SIZE, MOD_PANEL_C0 : MOD_PANEL_C0 + PANEL_SIZE]\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/edb79dae/29/code.py:205:    assert np.all(panel[3, :] == bg) and np.all(panel[:, 3] == bg), \"modifier panel must contain a background cross\"\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/edb79dae/29/code.py:208:        block = _extract_panel_block(panel, region)\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/edb79dae/29/code.py:231:    - The top-left corner contains a fixed legend rectangle made of two aligned 2x2 panels:\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/edb79dae/29/code.py:232:      a left base-color panel of solid swatches and a right modifier panel of glyphs.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/edb79dae/29/code.py:239:      Use that quadrant once to read a modifier glyph, use it again as the default base-panel index,\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/edb79dae/29/code.py:240:      apply the modifier to that quadrant index, and finally read the target color from the base panel.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/edb79dae/29/code.py:243:    Key insight: The left panel does not directly tell you each output color. Position chooses a base entry,\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/edb79dae/29/code.py:244:    but the right-panel glyph at the same position can redirect that lookup to another quadrant, so solving\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/edb79dae/29/code.py:252:    base_map = _read_base_panel(g, bg)\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/edb79dae/29/code.py:253:    modifier_map = _read_modifier_panel(g, bg)\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/edb79dae/29/code.py:346:def _base_panel(base_colors: dict[tuple[int, int], int], bg: int) -> np.ndarray:\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/edb79dae/29/code.py:347:    panel = np.full((PANEL_SIZE, PANEL_SIZE), bg, dtype=int)\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/edb79dae/29/code.py:350:        panel[r0 : r0 + PANEL_BLOCK, c0 : c0 + PANEL_BLOCK] = int(col)\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/edb79dae/29/code.py:351:    return panel\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/edb79dae/29/code.py:354:def _modifier_panel(region_to_delta: dict[tuple[int, int], tuple[int, int]], ink: int, bg: int) -> np.ndarray:\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/edb79dae/29/code.py:355:    panel = np.full((PANEL_SIZE, PANEL_SIZE), bg, dtype=int)\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/edb79dae/29/code.py:359:        panel[r0 : r0 + PANEL_BLOCK, c0 : c0 + PANEL_BLOCK][mask] = int(ink)\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/edb79dae/29/code.py:360:    return panel\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/edb79dae/29/code.py:367:    legend[:, :PANEL_SIZE] = _base_panel(base_colors, bg)\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/edb79dae/29/code.py:368:    legend[:, MOD_